// Satsang Diksha shlok texts — sanskrit (verse lines), gujarati (rendering),
// english (translation) + footnotes. Generated from Satsang_Diksha_Texts.json.
window.SD_TEXTS = {"1":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇah sākṣhād Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamah;","Sarvebhyah paramām shāntim ānandam sukham arpayet. 1"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān eṭale ke sākṣhāt Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārāj sarvane param shānti, ānand ane sukh arpe. (1)","english":"May Swaminarayan Bhagwan, that is, Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj himself,¹ bestow ultimate peace, bliss and happiness on all. (1)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["1. Here, Swaminarayan Bhagwan and Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj are synonyms and refer to the one supreme entity – Parabrahman, Paramatma."]},"2":{"sanskrit":["Deho’yam sādhanam mukter na bhoga-mātra-sādhanam;","Durlabho nashvarash-chā’yam vāram-vāram na labhyate. 2"],"gujarati":"Ā deh muktinu sādhan chhe, kevaḷ bhognu sādhan nathī. Durlabh ane nāshvant evo ā deh vāramvār maḷato nathī. (2)","english":"This body is a means for moksha, not merely a means for indulgence [in sense pleasures]. Rare and perishable, this body is not repeatedly attained. (2)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"3":{"sanskrit":["Laukiko vyavahāras-tu deha-nirvāha-hetukah;","Naiva sa paramam lakṣhyam asya manuṣhya-janmanaha. 3"],"gujarati":"Laukik vyavahār to dehnā nirvāh māṭe chhe. Te ā manuṣhya janmanu param lakṣhya nathī. (3)","english":"Personal and family activities are [only] for the sustenance of the body. They are not the ultimate objective of this human birth. (3)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"4":{"sanskrit":["Nāshāya sarva-doṣhāṇām brahma-sthiter avāptaye;","Kartum Bhagavato bhaktim asya dehasya lambhanam. 4"],"gujarati":"Sarva doṣhone ṭāḷavā, brahma-sthitine pāmavā ane Bhagwānnī bhakti karavā ā deh maḷyo chhe. Ā badhu satsang karavāthī avashya prāpta thāya chhe. Āthī mumukṣhuoe sadāya satsang karavo. (4-5)","english":"This body has been received to eradicate all flaws, attain the brāhmic state and offer devotion to Bhagwan. All this is certainly attained by practicing satsang.² Therefore, mumukshus should always practice satsang. (4–5)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["2. See verses 8–9 for a definition of ‘satsang.’"]},"5":{"sanskrit":["Sarvam idam hi satsangāl-labhyate nishchitam janaihi;","Atah sadaiva satsangah karaṇīyo mumukṣhubhihi. 5"],"gujarati":"Sarva doṣhone ṭāḷavā, brahma-sthitine pāmavā ane Bhagwānnī bhakti karavā ā deh maḷyo chhe. Ā badhu satsang karavāthī avashya prāpta thāya chhe. Āthī mumukṣhuoe sadāya satsang karavo. (4-5)","english":"This body has been received to eradicate all flaws, attain the brāhmic state and offer devotion to Bhagwan. All this is certainly attained by practicing satsang.² Therefore, mumukshus should always practice satsang. (4–5)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["2. See verses 8–9 for a definition of ‘satsang.’"]},"6":{"sanskrit":["Satsangah sthāpitas-tasmād divyo’yam parabrahmaṇā;","Swāminārāyaṇeneha sākṣhād evā’vatīrya cha. 6"],"gujarati":"Tethī Parabrahma Swāminārāyaṇe ā lokmā sākṣhāt avatarīne ā divya satsangnī sthāpanā karī. (6)","english":"For this reason, Parabrahman Swaminarayan himself manifested in this world and established this divine Satsang. (6)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"7":{"sanskrit":["Satsangasyā’sya vignānam mumukṣhūṇām bhaved iti;","Shāstram Satsanga-Dīkṣheti shubhā’shayād virachyate. 7"],"gujarati":"Ā satsangnu gnān mumukṣhuone thāya evā shubh āshayathī ‘Satsang-Dīkṣhā’ e nāmnu shāstra rachavāmā āve chhe. (7)","english":"The shastra titled ‘Satsang Diksha’ has been composed with the pure intent that mumukshus acquire the knowledge of this Satsang. (7)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"8":{"sanskrit":["Satyasya svātmanah sangah satyasya Paramātmanah;","Satyasya cha guroh sangah sach-chhāstrāṇām tathaiva cha. 8"],"gujarati":"Satya evā ātmāno sang karavo, satya evā Paramātmāno sang karavo, satya evā guruno sang karavo ane sachchhāstrano sang karavo e satsangnu sāchu lakṣhaṇ jāṇavu. Āvo divya satsang karanār manuṣhya sukhī thāy chhe. (8-9)","english":"One should know that the true meaning of satsang is to associate with the ātmā, which is true; to associate with Paramatma, who is true; to associate with the guru, who is true; and to associate with true shastras. One who practices this divine satsang becomes blissful. (8–9)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"9":{"sanskrit":["Vignātavyam idam satyam satsangasya hi lakṣhaṇam;","Kurvan-nevam vidham divyam satsangam syāt sukhī janaha. 9"],"gujarati":"Satya evā ātmāno sang karavo, satya evā Paramātmāno sang karavo, satya evā guruno sang karavo ane sachchhāstrano sang karavo e satsangnu sāchu lakṣhaṇ jāṇavu. Āvo divya satsang karanār manuṣhya sukhī thāy chhe. (8-9)","english":"One should know that the true meaning of satsang is to associate with the ātmā, which is true; to associate with Paramatma, who is true; to associate with the guru, who is true; and to associate with true shastras. One who practices this divine satsang becomes blissful. (8–9)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"10":{"sanskrit":["Dīkṣheti dṛuḍha-sankalpah sa-shraddham nishchayo’chalaha;","Samyak samarpaṇam prītyā niṣhṭhā vratam dṛuḍhāshrayaha. 10"],"gujarati":"Dīkṣhā eṭale dṛuḍh sankalp, shraddhāe sahit evo achaḷ nishchay, samyak samarpaṇ, prīti-pūrvak niṣhṭhā, vrat ane dṛuḍh āsharo. (10)","english":"‘Diksha’ means firm resolve, unwavering conviction coupled with faith, absolute dedication, loving faith, observances and firm refuge. (10)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"11":{"sanskrit":["Shāstre’smin gnāpitā spaṣhṭam āgnopāsana-paddhatihi;","Paramātma-Parabrahma-Sahajānanda-darshitā. 11"],"gujarati":"Ā shāstramā Parabrahma Sahajānand Paramātmāe darshāvel āgnā tathā upāsanānī paddhatine spaṣhṭa rīte jaṇāvī chhe. (11)","english":"The methods of āgnā and upāsanā revealed by Parabrahman Sahajanand Paramatma are clearly expressed in this shastra. (11)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"12":{"sanskrit":["Satsangā’dhikṛutah sarve sarve sukhā’dhi-kāriṇaha;","Sarve’rhā brahmavidyāyām nāryash-chaiva narās-tathā. 12"],"gujarati":"Puruṣho tathā strīo sarve satsangnā adhikārī chhe, sarve sukhnā adhikārī chhe ane sarve brahma-vidyānā adhikārī chhe. (12)","english":"All males and females are entitled to satsang, all are entitled to happiness and all are entitled to brahmavidyā. (12)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"13":{"sanskrit":["Naiva nyūnādhikatvam syāt satsange linga-bhedataha;","Sva-sva-maryādayā sarve bhaktyā muktim samāpnuyuhu. 13"],"gujarati":"Satsangmā ling-bhedthī nyūnādhikpaṇu na ja samajavu. Badhā pot-potānī maryādāmā rahī bhakti vaḍe muktine pāmī shake chhe. (13)","english":"In Satsang, superiority or inferiority should never be understood to be based on gender. All can attain moksha through devotion while observing the dharma prescribed for them. (13)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"14":{"sanskrit":["Sarva-varṇa-gatāh sarvā nāryah sarve narās-tathā;","Satsange brahmavidyāyām mokṣhe sadā’dhikāriṇaha. 14"],"gujarati":"Sarva varṇanā sarva strīo tathā sarva puruṣho sadāy satsang, brahma-vidyā ane mokṣhanā adhikārī chhe. Varṇanā ādhāre kyārey nyūnādhik-bhāv na karavo. Sarva janoe potānā varṇanu mān tyajīne paraspar sevā karavī. Jātie karīne koī mahān nathī ane koī nyūn paṇ nathī. Tethī nāt-jātne laīne klesh na karavo ne sukhe satsang karavo. (14-16)","english":"All men and women of all castes are forever entitled to satsang, brahmavidyā and moksha. Do not attribute notions of superiority and inferiority based on varna. All persons should shun their ego based on their caste and serve one another. No one is superior and no one is inferior by birth. Therefore, one should not quarrel based on caste or class and should joyfully practice satsang. (14–16)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"15":{"sanskrit":["Na nyūnā’dhikatā kāryā varṇā’dhāreṇa karhichit;","Tyaktvā sva-varṇa-mānam cha sevā kāryā mithah samaihi. 15"],"gujarati":"Sarva varṇanā sarva strīo tathā sarva puruṣho sadāy satsang, brahma-vidyā ane mokṣhanā adhikārī chhe. Varṇanā ādhāre kyārey nyūnādhik-bhāv na karavo. Sarva janoe potānā varṇanu mān tyajīne paraspar sevā karavī. Jātie karīne koī mahān nathī ane koī nyūn paṇ nathī. Tethī nāt-jātne laīne klesh na karavo ne sukhe satsang karavo. (14-16)","english":"All men and women of all castes are forever entitled to satsang, brahmavidyā and moksha. Do not attribute notions of superiority and inferiority based on varna. All persons should shun their ego based on their caste and serve one another. No one is superior and no one is inferior by birth. Therefore, one should not quarrel based on caste or class and should joyfully practice satsang. (14–16)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"16":{"sanskrit":["Jātyā naiva mahān ko’pi naiva nyūnas-tathā yataha;","Jātyā klesho na kartavyah sukham satsangam ācharet. 16"],"gujarati":"Sarva varṇanā sarva strīo tathā sarva puruṣho sadāy satsang, brahma-vidyā ane mokṣhanā adhikārī chhe. Varṇanā ādhāre kyārey nyūnādhik-bhāv na karavo. Sarva janoe potānā varṇanu mān tyajīne paraspar sevā karavī. Jātie karīne koī mahān nathī ane koī nyūn paṇ nathī. Tethī nāt-jātne laīne klesh na karavo ne sukhe satsang karavo. (14-16)","english":"All men and women of all castes are forever entitled to satsang, brahmavidyā and moksha. Do not attribute notions of superiority and inferiority based on varna. All persons should shun their ego based on their caste and serve one another. No one is superior and no one is inferior by birth. Therefore, one should not quarrel based on caste or class and should joyfully practice satsang. (14–16)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"17":{"sanskrit":["Sarve’dhikāriṇo mokṣhe gṛuhiṇas-tyāgino’pi cha;","Na nyūnā’dhikatā tatra sarve bhaktā yatah Prabhoho. 17"],"gujarati":"Gṛuhasth tathā tyāgī sarve mokṣhanā adhikārī chhe. Temā nyūnādhik-bhāv nathī, kāraṇ ke gṛuhasth ke tyāgī badhā Bhagwānnā bhakto chhe. (17)","english":"Householders and renunciants are all entitled to moksha. Between them neither is inferior or superior, because householders and renunciants are all devotees of Bhagwan. (17)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"18":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇe’nanya-dṛuḍha-parama-bhaktaye;","Gṛuhītvā’shraya-dīkṣhāyā mantram satsangam āpnuyāt. 18"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānne viṣhe ananya, dṛuḍh ane param bhakti māṭe āshraya-dīkṣhā-mantra grahaṇ karī satsang prāpta karavo. (18)","english":"To offer singular, resolute and supreme devotion to Bhagwan Swaminarayan, one should receive the Ashray Diksha Mantra³ and affiliate with the Satsang. (18)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["3. ‘Ashray Diksha Mantra’ refers to a specific mantra recited when one first takes refuge in Satsang."]},"19":{"sanskrit":["Dhanyo’smi pūrṇakāmo’smi niṣhpāpo nirbhayah sukhī;","Akṣhara-guru-yogena Swāminārāyaṇā’shrayāt. 19"],"gujarati":"Āshraya-dīkṣhā mantra ā pramāṇe chhe:\nDhanyosmi pūrṇakāmosmi niṣhpāpo nirbhayah sukhī;\nAkṣhara-guru-yogena Swāminārāyaṇ-āshrayāt.¹ (19)","english":"The Ashray Diksha Mantra is as follows:\nDhanyo’smi purna-kāmo’smi\nnishpāpo nirbhayah sukhi;\nAkshara-guru-yogena\nSwaminārāyan-āshrayat.⁴ (19)","gujFoot":["1. Mantra upar lakhyā pramāṇe ja bolavo. Mantrano tātparyārth ā pramāṇe chhe: Akṣharbrahma gurunā yoge Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānno āsharo karavāthī hu dhanya chhu, pūrṇakām chhu, niṣhpāp, nirbhay ane sukhī chhu."],"engFoot":["4. This mantra should be recited as written. The meaning of this mantra is as follows: “Having taken refuge in Swaminarayan Bhagwan through the association of the Aksharbrahman guru, I am blessed, I am fulfilled, I am without sins, I am fearless and I am blissful.”"]},"20":{"sanskrit":["Āshrayet Sahajānandam Harim Brahmā’kṣharam tathā;","Guṇātītam gurum prītyā mumukṣhuh svātma-muktaye. 20"],"gujarati":"Mumukṣhu potānā ātmānī mukti māṭe Sahajānand Shrīhari tathā Akṣharbrahma swarūp guṇātīt guruno prītie karīne āsharo kare. (20)","english":"For the moksha of one’s ātmā, a mumukshu should lovingly take refuge of Sahajanand Shri Hari and the Aksharbrahman Gunatit guru.⁵ (20)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["5. ‘Gunatit guru’ refers to the Aksharbrahman guru, who is beyond māyā."]},"21":{"sanskrit":["Kāṣhṭha-jām dvi-guṇām mālām kaṇṭhe sadaiva dhārayet;","Satsangam hi samāshritya satsanga-niyamāns-tathā. 21"],"gujarati":"Satsangno āsharo karī sadāy kanṭhne viṣhe kāṣhṭhnī bevaḍī māḷā dhāraṇ karavī tathā satsangnā niyamo dhāraṇ karavā. (21)","english":"Upon taking the refuge of satsang, one should always wear a double-stranded wooden kanthi around the neck and accept the niyams of satsang. (21)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"22":{"sanskrit":["Gurum Brahmaswarūpam tu vinā na sambhaved bhave;","Tattvato brahmavidyāyāh sākṣhātkāro hi jīvane. 22"],"gujarati":"Ā sansārmā brahmaswarūp guru vinā jīvanmā brahma-vidyāno tattve karīne sākṣhātkār na thaī shake. (22)","english":"In this world, brahmavidyā cannot be fully realized in life without the Brahmaswarup guru.⁶ (22)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["6. ‘Brahmaswarup guru’ refers to the Aksharbrahman guru."]},"23":{"sanskrit":["Nottamo nirvikalpash-cha nishchayah Paramātmanaha;","Na svātma-brahma-bhāvo’pi Brahmā’kṣharam gurum vinā. 23"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahma guru vinā Paramātmāno uttam nirvikalp nishchay na thaī shake tathā potānā ātmāne viṣhe brahmabhāv paṇ prāpta na thaī shake. (23)","english":"Without the Aksharbrahman guru, supreme, unwavering conviction (nishchay) in Paramatma cannot be attained and one’s ātmā also cannot acquire brahmabhāv. (23)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"24":{"sanskrit":["Naivā’pi tattvato bhaktih paramānanda-prāpaṇam;","Nā’pi trividha-tāpānām nāsho Brahma-gurum vinā. 24"],"gujarati":"Brahmaswarūp guru vinā yathārth bhakti paṇ na thaī shake, param ānandnī prāpti na thāy ane trividh tāpano nāsh paṇ na thāy. (24)","english":"Without the Brahmaswarup guru, perfect devotion also cannot be offered, ultimate bliss cannot be attained and the three types of misery⁷ also cannot be eradicated. (24)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["7. The three types of misery are those that stem from other beings, the deities and personal shortcomings."]},"25":{"sanskrit":["Atah samāshrayen-nityam pratyakṣham Akṣharam gurum;","Sarva-siddhi-karam divyam Paramātmā’nubhāvakam. 25"],"gujarati":"Āthī sarva arthnī siddhi kare tathā Paramātmāno anubhav karāve tevā pratyakṣh Akṣharbrahma guruno āsharo sadāy karavo. (25)","english":"Therefore, one should always take the refuge of the manifest Aksharbrahman guru, who enables one to attain all objectives and experience Paramatma. (25)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"26":{"sanskrit":["Sarvam dur-vyasanam tyājyam sarvaih satsangibhih sadā;","Aneka-roga-dukhānām kāraṇam vyasanam yataha. 26"],"gujarati":"Sarva satsangīoe sarve durvyasanono sadāy tyāg karavo. Kāraṇ ke vyasan anek rogonu tathā dukhonu kāraṇ bane chhe. (26)","english":"All satsangis should always renounce all harmful addictions, as addictions cause numerous illnesses and miseries. (26)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"27":{"sanskrit":["Surā-bhangā-tamālādi yad yad bhaveddhi mādakam;","Tad bhakṣhayet piben-naiva dhūmra-pānam api tyajet. 27"],"gujarati":"Surā, bhāng tathā tamāku ityādi je je padārtho mādak hoy te kyārey khāvā ke pīvā nahī tathā dhūmra-pānno paṇ tyāg karavo. (27)","english":"One should never consume intoxicating substances, such as alcohol, bhang and tobacco. One should also refrain from smoking. (27)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"28":{"sanskrit":["Pari-tyājyam sadā dyūtam sarvaih sarva-prakārakam;","Tyaktavyo vyabhichārash-cha nārībhih puruṣhais-tathā. 28"],"gujarati":"Sarve strī tathā puruṣhoe sarva prakārnā jugārno tathā vyabhichārno tyāg karavo. (28)","english":"All women and men should never engage in any form of gambling or adultery. (28)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"29":{"sanskrit":["Mānsam matsyam tathā’ṇḍāni bhakṣhayeyur na karhichit;","Palāṇḍum lashunam hingu na cha satsangino janāhā. 29"],"gujarati":"Satsangī janoe kyārey māns, māchhalī, īnḍā tathā ḍungaḷī, lasaṇ, hing na khāvā. (29)","english":"Satsangis should never eat meat, fish, eggs, onions, garlic or hing. (29)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"30":{"sanskrit":["Pātavyam gālitam peyam jalam dugdhādikam tathā;","Khādyam pānam ashuddham yad gṛuhṇīyād vastu tan-nahi. 30"],"gujarati":"Pāṇī tathā dūdh ityādi peya padārtho gāḷelā grahaṇ karavā. Je khādya vastu tathā pīṇā ashuddha hoy te kyārey grahaṇ na karavā. (30)","english":"One should consume water, milk and other drinkable items [only] after they have been filtered. Food items and beverages that are forbidden should never be consumed. (30)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"31":{"sanskrit":["Chauryam na karhichit kāryam satsangam āshritair janaihi;","Dharmārtham api no kāryam chora-kāryam tu karhichit. 31"],"gujarati":"Satsangīoe chorī kyārey na karavī. Dharmane arthe paṇ chorī kyārey na karavī. (31)","english":"Satsangis should never steal. Even for the sake of dharma, one should never commit theft. (31)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"32":{"sanskrit":["Naivā’nya-svāmikam grāhyam tad-anugnām vinā svayam;","Puṣhpa-falādyapi vastu sūkṣhma-chauryam tad uchyate. 32"],"gujarati":"Puṣhp, faḷo jevī vastu paṇ tenā dhaṇīnī paravāngī vagar na levī. Paravāngī vagar levu te sūkṣhma chorī kahevāy chhe. (32)","english":"One should never take even objects such as flowers or fruits without the consent of their owners. Taking without consent is a subtle form of theft. (32)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"33":{"sanskrit":["Manuṣhyāṇām pashūnām vā matkuṇādesh-cha pakṣhiṇām;","Keṣhānchij-jīva-jantūnām hinsā kāryā na karhichit. 33"],"gujarati":"Kyārey manuṣhya, pashu, pakṣhī, tathā mānkaḍ ādik koī paṇ jīv-jantuonī hinsā na karavī. Ahinsā param dharma chhe, hinsā adharma chhe em Shruti-Smṛutyādi shāstromā spaṣhṭa kahevāmā āvyu chhe. (33-34)","english":"One should never kill humans, animals, birds and bugs or other insects and creatures. The Shrutis, Smrutis and other sacred texts clearly describe non-violence as the highest dharma and violence as adharma. (33–34)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"34":{"sanskrit":["Ahinsā paramo dharmo hinsā tvadharma-rūpiṇī;","Shruti-smṛutyādi-shāstreṣhu sfuṭam evam prakīrtitam. 34"],"gujarati":"Kyārey manuṣhya, pashu, pakṣhī, tathā mānkaḍ ādik koī paṇ jīv-jantuonī hinsā na karavī. Ahinsā param dharma chhe, hinsā adharma chhe em Shruti-Smṛutyādi shāstromā spaṣhṭa kahevāmā āvyu chhe. (33-34)","english":"One should never kill humans, animals, birds and bugs or other insects and creatures. The Shrutis, Smrutis and other sacred texts clearly describe non-violence as the highest dharma and violence as adharma. (33–34)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"35":{"sanskrit":["Yāgārtham apyajādīnām nirdoṣhāṇām hi prāṇinām;","Hinsanam naiva kartavyam satsangibhihi kadāchana. 35"],"gujarati":"Satsangīoe yagnane arthe paṇ bakarā vagere nirdoṣh prāṇīonī hinsā kyārey na ja karavī. (35)","english":"Even for a yagna, satsangis should never harm goats or any other innocent animals. (35)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"36":{"sanskrit":["Yāgādike cha kartavye siddhāntam sāmpradāyikam;","Anusṛutya hi kartavyam hinsā-rahitam eva tat. 36"],"gujarati":"Yāgādi karavānā thāy tyāre sampradāynā siddhāntne anusarīne hinsā-rahit ja karavā. (36)","english":"When yagnas are held, they should only be conducted without harming any beings and according to the Sampraday’s principles. (36)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"37":{"sanskrit":["Matvā’pi yagna-sheṣham cha vā’pi deva-niveditam;","Mānsam kadāpi bhakṣhyam na satsangam āshritair-janaihi. 37"],"gujarati":"Yagnano sheṣh gaṇīne ke pachhī devatānā naivedya rūpe paṇ satsangīoe kyārey māns na ja khāvu. (37)","english":"Satsangis should never eat meat, even if it is considered to be the remnant of a yagna or sanctified by the deities. (37)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"38":{"sanskrit":["Kasyā’pi tāḍanam naiva karaṇīyam kadāchana;","Apa-shabdā’pamānādi-sūkṣhma-hinsā’pi naiva cha. 38"],"gujarati":"Koīnu tāḍan kyārey na karavu. Apshabdo kahevā, apamān karavu ityādi koīpaṇ prakāre sūkṣhma hinsā paṇ na karavī. (38)","english":"One should never strike another person. One should not swear, insult or commit other forms of subtle harm or injury. (38)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"39":{"sanskrit":["Sattā-kīrti-dhana-dravya-strī-puruṣhādikā’ptaye;","Mānerṣhyā-krodhatash-chā’pi hinsām naiva samācharet. 39"],"gujarati":"Dhan, sattā, kīrti, strī, puruṣh ityādinī prāptine arthe tathā mān, īrṣhyā ke krodhe karīne paṇ hinsā na karavī. (39)","english":"One should not commit violence to attain wealth, power, prestige or [to fulfil one’s desire] for a man or woman or anything else. Also, one should also not commit violence out of ego, jealousy or anger. (39)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"40":{"sanskrit":["Manasā vachasā vā’pi karmaṇā hinsane kṛute;","Tat-sthito dukhyate nūnam Swāminārāyaṇo Harihi. 40"],"gujarati":"Mane karīne, vachane karīne ke karme karīne hinsā karavāthī tenāmā rahelā Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān dukhāy chhe. (40)","english":"Inflicting mental, verbal or physical violence pains Swaminarayan Bhagwan, who resides within that person. (40)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"41":{"sanskrit":["Ātma-ghāto’pi hinsaiva na kāryo’tah kadāchana;","Patana-gala-bandhādyair viṣha-bhakṣhādibhis-tathā. 41"],"gujarati":"Ātma-hatyā karavī te paṇ hinsā ja chhe. Āthī paḍatu mūkavu, gaḷe ṭūnpo khāvo, zer khāvu ityādi koī rīte ātma-hatyā kyārey na karavī. (41)","english":"Suicide is also a form of violence. Therefore, never commit suicide by falling from heights, hanging oneself, consuming poison or any other means. (41)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"42":{"sanskrit":["Dukha-lajjā-bhaya-krodha-rogādyāpatti kāraṇāt;","Dharmā’rtham api kashchiddhi hanyān-na swam na vā param. 42"],"gujarati":"Dukh, lajjā, bhay, krodh tathā rog ityādi āpattine kāraṇe, ke pachhī dharmane arthe paṇ koīe potānī ke anyanī hatyā na karavī. (42)","english":"No one should kill oneself or others out of grief, shame, fear, anger or due to illness and other adversities, not even for the sake of dharma. (42)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"43":{"sanskrit":["Tīrthe’pi naiva kartavya ātma-ghāto mumukṣhubhihi;","Naivā’pi mokṣha-puṇyāpti bhāvāt kāryah sa tatra cha. 43"],"gujarati":"Mumukṣhue tīrthane viṣhe paṇ ātma-hatyā na ja karavī. Mokṣha ke puṇya pāmavānī bhāvanāthī paṇ tīrthane viṣhe āpghāt na ja karavo. (43)","english":"A mumukshu should never commit suicide even at a place of pilgrimage. One should never commit suicide at pilgrimage places even with the hope of attaining moksha or merits. (43)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"44":{"sanskrit":["Bhagavān sarva-kartā’sti dayāluh sarva-rakṣhakaha;","Sa eva nāshakah sarva-sankaṭānām sadā mama. 44"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān sarva-kartā chhe, dayāḷu chhe, sarvanu rakṣhaṇ karanārā chhe ane e ja sadā mārā sarve sankaṭonā ṭāḷanārā chhe. (44)","english":"Bhagwan is the all-doer, compassionate and the protector of all; at all times, he alone is the resolver of all my adversities. (44)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"45":{"sanskrit":["Bhagavān kurute yaddhi hitārtham eva tat sadā;","Prārabdham me tad ichchhaiva sa eva tārako mama. 45"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān je kare te sadāy sārā māṭe hoy. Temanī ichchhā e ja māru prārabdha chhe. Teo ja mārā tārak chhe. (45)","english":"Whatever Bhagwan does is always beneficial. His wish alone is my prārabdh. He alone is my liberator. (45)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"46":{"sanskrit":["Nūnam nankṣhyanti me vighnāh pāpa-doṣhāsh-cha dur-guṇāhā;","Nūnam prāpsyāmyaham shāntim ānandam paramam sukham. 46"],"gujarati":"Mārā vighno, pāp, doṣh tathā durguṇo avashya nāsh pāmashe. Hu avashya shānti, param ānand ane sukh pāmīsh. (46)","english":"My hindrances, sins, flaws and bad qualities will certainly be destroyed. I will surely attain peace, supreme bliss and happiness. (46)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"47":{"sanskrit":["Yato mām militah sākṣhād Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamaha;","Nishchayena tariṣhyāmi dukha-jātam hi tad balāt. 47"],"gujarati":"Kāraṇ ke mane sākṣhāt Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārāj maḷyā chhe. Temanā baḷe hu jarūr dukhne tarī jaīsh. (47)","english":"This is because I have attained the manifest form of Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj. With his strength, I will surely overcome misery. (47)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"48":{"sanskrit":["Vichāryaivam balam rakṣhed nā’shrito nirbalo bhavet;","Ānandito bhaven-nityam Bhagavad bala vaibhavāt. 48"],"gujarati":"Ā rīte vichārnu baḷ rākhī āshrit bhakta kyārey himmat na hāre ane Bhagwānnā baḷe ānandmā rahe. (48)","english":"With the strength of such thoughts, a devotee who has taken refuge never loses courage and remains joyous due to the strength of Bhagwan. (48)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"49":{"sanskrit":["Ṣhṭhīvanam mala-mūtrādi-visarjanam sthaleṣhu cha;","Shāstra-loka-niṣhiddheṣhu na kartavyam kadāchana. 49"],"gujarati":"Shāstramā tathā lokmā niṣhedh karyo hoy tevā sthānone viṣhe kyārey thūnkavu nahī tathā maḷ-mūtrādi na karavu. (49)","english":"One should never spit, urinate or defecate in places prohibited by the shastras and society. (49)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"50":{"sanskrit":["Shuddhih sarvavidhā pālyā bāhyā chā’bhyantarā sadā;","Shuddhi-priyah prasīdech-cha shuddhi-mati jane Harihi. 50"],"gujarati":"Bāhya ane āntarik em sarva prakārnī shuddhinu pālan karavu. Shrīharine shuddhi priya chhe ane shuddhivāḷā manuṣhyanī upar teo prasanna thāy chhe. (50)","english":"One should observe all forms of external and internal purity. Shri Hari⁸ loves purity and is pleased with those who are pure. (50)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["8. ‘Shri Hari’ is another name for Bhagwan Swaminarayan."]},"51":{"sanskrit":["Satsangibhih praboddhavyam pūrvam sūryodayāt sadā;","Tatah snānādikam kṛutvā dhartavyam shuddha vastrakam. 51"],"gujarati":"Satsangīoe sadā sūrya ūgyā pūrve jāgavu. Tyār bād snānādik karī shuddha vastro dhāraṇ karavā. (51)","english":"Satsangis should always wake up before sunrise. After bathing and other morning routines, they should put on clean clothes. (51)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"52":{"sanskrit":["Pūrvasyām uttarasyām vā dishi kṛutvā mukham tataha;","Shuddhā’sanopaviṣhṭah san-nitya-pūjām samācharet. 52"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād pūrva dishāmā athavā uttar dishāmā mukh rākhī, shuddha āsan upar besī nitya-pūjā karavī. (52)","english":"Thereafter, one should sit on a clean āsan and perform personal daily puja facing east or north. (52)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"53":{"sanskrit":["Prabhu-pūjopa-yuktena chandanenordhva puṇḍrakam;","Bhāle hi tilakam kuryāt kumkumena cha chandrakam. 53"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ mantrano jāp karatā tathā gurunu smaraṇ karatā karatā bhālne viṣhe Bhagwānnī pūjāthī prasādībhūt thayel chandan vaḍe ūrdhva-punḍra tilak karavu ane kumkum vaḍe chāndalo karavo tathā chhātī ane banne bhujāo par chandanthī tilak-chāndalo karavo. (53-54)","english":"While chanting the Swaminarayan mantra and remembering the guru, apply a U-shaped tilak made from chandan that has been sanctified by having been offered to Bhagwan and a kumkum chandlo to the forehead. One should also apply a tilak-chandlo of chandan to the chest and both arms. (53–54)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"54":{"sanskrit":["Urasi hastayosh-chandram tilakam chandanena cha;","Swāminārāyaṇam mantram japan kuryād gurum smaran. 54"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ mantrano jāp karatā tathā gurunu smaraṇ karatā karatā bhālne viṣhe Bhagwānnī pūjāthī prasādībhūt thayel chandan vaḍe ūrdhva-punḍra tilak karavu ane kumkum vaḍe chāndalo karavo tathā chhātī ane banne bhujāo par chandanthī tilak-chāndalo karavo. (53-54)","english":"While chanting the Swaminarayan mantra and remembering the guru, apply a U-shaped tilak made from chandan that has been sanctified by having been offered to Bhagwan and a kumkum chandlo to the forehead. One should also apply a tilak-chandlo of chandan to the chest and both arms. (53–54)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"55":{"sanskrit":["Kevalam chandrakah strībhih kartavyas-tilakam na hi;","Kumkuma dravyato bhāle smarantībhir harim gurum. 55"],"gujarati":"Strīoe Bhagwān tathā gurunu smaraṇ karatā bhālne viṣhe kevaḷ kumkumno chāndalo karavo. Tilak na karavu. (55)","english":"While remembering Bhagwan and the guru, women should imprint only a kumkum chandlo to their foreheads. They should not apply a tilak. (55)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"56":{"sanskrit":["Tatah pūjā’dhikārāya bhaktah satsangam āshritaha;","Kuryād ātma-vichāram cha pratāpam chintayan harehe. 56"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād satsangne āshrit bhakte pūjānā adhikār māṭe Bhagwānnā pratāpnu chintavan karatā karatā ātma-vichār karavo. Prasanna chitte ane bhakti-bhāv-pūrvak ‘Akṣharam aham Puruṣhottama-dāsosmi’ e pavitra mantranu uchchāraṇ karavu. Potānā ātmāne viṣhe Akṣharbrahmanī vibhāvanā karavī ane shānt thaī, ekāgra chitte mānasī pūjā karavī. (56-58)","english":"Thereafter, to gain the privilege to perform puja, a devotee who has taken the refuge of satsang should meditate on their ātmā while contemplating upon the glory of Bhagwan. The sacred mantra ‘Aksharam-aham Purushottam-dāso’smi’ should be recited with joy and devotion. One should identify one’s ātmā with Aksharbrahman and perform mānsi puja with a calm and focused mind. (56–58)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"57":{"sanskrit":["Akṣharam-aham ityevam bhaktyā prasanna chetasā;","Puruṣhottama dāso’smi mantram etam vadech-chhuchim. 57"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād satsangne āshrit bhakte pūjānā adhikār māṭe Bhagwānnā pratāpnu chintavan karatā karatā ātma-vichār karavo. Prasanna chitte ane bhakti-bhāv-pūrvak ‘Akṣharam aham Puruṣhottama-dāsosmi’ e pavitra mantranu uchchāraṇ karavu. Potānā ātmāne viṣhe Akṣharbrahmanī vibhāvanā karavī ane shānt thaī, ekāgra chitte mānasī pūjā karavī. (56-58)","english":"Thereafter, to gain the privilege to perform puja, a devotee who has taken the refuge of satsang should meditate on their ātmā while contemplating upon the glory of Bhagwan. The sacred mantra ‘Aksharam-aham Purushottam-dāso’smi’ should be recited with joy and devotion. One should identify one’s ātmā with Aksharbrahman and perform mānsi puja with a calm and focused mind. (56–58)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"58":{"sanskrit":["Akṣharabrahma rūpatvam svasyā’tmani vibhāvayet;","Kuryāch-cha mānasīm pūjām shānta ekāgra chetasā. 58"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād satsangne āshrit bhakte pūjānā adhikār māṭe Bhagwānnā pratāpnu chintavan karatā karatā ātma-vichār karavo. Prasanna chitte ane bhakti-bhāv-pūrvak ‘Akṣharam aham Puruṣhottama-dāsosmi’² e pavitra mantranu uchchāraṇ karavu. Potānā ātmāne viṣhe Akṣharbrahmanī vibhāvanā karavī ane shānt thaī, ekāgra chitte mānasī pūjā karavī. (56-58)","english":"Thereafter, to gain the privilege to perform puja, a devotee who has taken the refuge of satsang should meditate on their ātmā while contemplating upon the glory of Bhagwan. The sacred mantra ‘Aksharam-aham Purushottam-dāso’smi’⁹ should be recited with joy and devotion. One should identify one’s ātmā with Aksharbrahman and perform mānsi puja with a calm and focused mind. (56–58)","gujFoot":["2. Mantra upar lakhyā pramāṇe ja bolavo. Mantrano tātparyārth ā pramāṇe chhe: Akṣhar evo hu Puruṣhottamno dās chhu."],"engFoot":["9. This mantra should be recited as written. The meaning of this mantra is as follows: “I am akshar, a servant of Purushottam.”"]},"59":{"sanskrit":["Harir Brahma-gurush-chaiva bhavato mokṣha-dāyakau;","Tayor eva hi kartavyam dhyānam mānasa-pūjanam. 59"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān ane brahmaswarūp guru ja mokṣha-dātā chhe. Temanā ja dhyān tathā mānasī pūjā karavā. (59)","english":"Only Bhagwan and the Brahmaswarup guru can bestow moksha. Therefore, one should only meditate upon them and perform their mānsi puja. (59)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"60":{"sanskrit":["Sthāpayech-chitra-mūrtīsh-cha shuchi vastropari tataha;","Darshanam syād yathā samyak tathā hi bhakti-bhāvataha. 60"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād pavitra vastra upar chitra-pratimāonu sārī rīte darshan thāy tem bhakti-bhāv-pūrvak sthāpan karavu. (60)","english":"Thereafter, devoutly place the pictorial murtis on a clean cloth in a way that one can easily do their darshan. (60)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"61":{"sanskrit":["Madhye tu sthāpayet tatra hyakṣhara-Puruṣhottamau;","Swāminam hi Guṇātītam Mahārājam cha tat param. 61"],"gujarati":"Temā madhyamā Akṣhar tathā Puruṣhottamnī mūrti padharāvavī eṭale ke Guṇātītānand Swāmī tathā temanāthī par evā Mahārājne padharāvavā. (61)","english":"In the center, one should arrange the murtis of Akshar and Purushottam, that is, Gunatitanand Swami and the one who transcends him, [Shriji] Maharaj. (61)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"62":{"sanskrit":["Pramukha-Swāmi-paryantam pratyeka-guru-mūrtayaha;","Prasthāpyāh sevitānām cha pratyakṣham mūrtayah svayam. 62"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād Pramukh Swāmī Mahārāj paryant pratyek guruonī mūrtio padharāvavī tathā pote pratyakṣh sevyā hoy te guruonī mūrtio padharāvavī. (62)","english":"One should then place the murtis of each guru up to Pramukh Swami Maharaj and the murtis of the gurus whom one has personally served. (62)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"63":{"sanskrit":["Āhvāna-shlokam uchchārya Harim cha gurum āhvayet;","Hastau baddhvā namaskāram kuryāddhi dāsa-bhāvataha. 63"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād āhvān shlok bolīne Mahārāj tathā Guruonu āhvān karavu. Be hāth joḍī dāsbhāve namaskār karavā. (63)","english":"Thereafter, one should invite [Shriji] Maharaj and the gurus by reciting the Ahvan Mantra.¹⁰ One should bow with folded hands and with dāsbhāv. (63)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["10. The Ahvan Mantra is a verse recited to invite Bhagwan into one’s puja."]},"64":{"sanskrit":["Uttiṣhṭha Sahajānanda Shrī-Hare Puruṣhottama;","Guṇātītā’kṣhara Brahmann-uttiṣhṭha kṛupayā guro. 64"],"gujarati":"Āhvān mantra ā pramāṇe chhe:\nUttiṣhṭha Sahajānanda Shrī-Hare Puruṣhottama;\nGuṇātītākṣhara brahmann-uttiṣhṭha kṛupayā guro.\nĀgamyatām hi pūjārtham āgamyatām mad-ātmatah;\nSānnidhyād darshanād divyāt saubhāgyam vardhate mama. (64-65)","english":"The Ahvan Mantra is as follows:\nUttishtha Sahajānanda Shri-Hare Purushottama;\nGunātitā’kshara brahmann-uttishtha krupayā guro.\nĀgamyatām hi pujārtham āgamyatām mad-ātmataha;\nSānnidhyād darshanād divyāt saubhāgyam vardhate mama. (64–65)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"65":{"sanskrit":["Āgamyatām hi pūjārtham āgamyatām mad-ātmataha;","Sānnidhyād darshanād divyāt saubhāgyam vardhate mama. 65"],"gujarati":"Āhvān mantra ā pramāṇe chhe:\nUttiṣhṭha Sahajānanda Shrī-Hare Puruṣhottama;\nGuṇātītākṣhara brahmann-uttiṣhṭha kṛupayā guro.\nĀgamyatām hi pūjārtham āgamyatām mad-ātmatah;\nSānnidhyād darshanād divyāt saubhāgyam vardhate mama.³ (64-65)","english":"The Ahvan Mantra is as follows:\nUttishtha Sahajānanda Shri-Hare Purushottama;\nGunātitā’kshara brahmann-uttishtha krupayā guro.\nĀgamyatām hi pujārtham āgamyatām mad-ātmataha;\nSānnidhyād darshanād divyāt saubhāgyam vardhate mama.¹¹ (64–65)","gujFoot":["3. Mantra upar lakhyā pramāṇe ja bolavo. Mantrano tātparyārth ā pramāṇe chhe: He Sahajānand Shrī Hari! He Puruṣhottam! Kṛupā karīne uṭho. He Akṣharbrahma Guṇātīt guru! Kṛupā karīne uṭho. Mārī pūjā svīkāravā māṭe mārā ātmāmāthī padhāro. Āpanā divya sānnidhya ane darshanthī māru saubhāgya vadhe chhe."],"engFoot":["11. This mantra should be recited as written. The meaning of this mantra is as follows: “O Sahajanand Shri Hari! O Purushottam! O Aksharbrahman Gunatit gurus! Please shower compassion [upon me] and awaken. Please come forth from my ātmā, to accept my puja. I become more blessed due to your divine presence and darshan.”"]},"66":{"sanskrit":["Mālām āvartayed mantram Swāminārāyaṇam japan;","Mahimnā darshanam kurvan mūrtīnām sthira-chetasā. 66"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād sthir chitte tathā mahimā sāthe mūrtionā darshan karatā karatā Swāminārāyaṇ mantrano jāp karatā māḷā feravavī. Tyār bād ek page ūbhā rahī, hāth ūnchā rākhī mūrtionā darshan karatā tapnī māḷā feravavī. (66-67)","english":"Thereafter, with mahimā and a steady mind, one should perform mālā while chanting the Swaminarayan mantra and having darshan of the murtis. Afterwards, while continuing to do darshan of the murtis, one should stand on one leg with arms raised and perform tapni mālā. (66–67)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"67":{"sanskrit":["Eka-pādotthito bhūtvā mālām āvartayet tataha;","Tapasa ūrdhva-hastah san kurvāṇo mūrti-darshanam. 67"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād sthir chitte tathā mahimā sāthe mūrtionā darshan karatā karatā Swāminārāyaṇ mantrano jāp karatā māḷā feravavī. Tyār bād ek page ūbhā rahī, hāth ūnchā rākhī mūrtionā darshan karatā tapnī māḷā feravavī. (66-67)","english":"Thereafter, with mahimā and a steady mind, one should perform mālā while chanting the Swaminarayan mantra and having darshan of the murtis. Afterwards, while continuing to do darshan of the murtis, one should stand on one leg with arms raised and perform tapni mālā. (66–67)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"68":{"sanskrit":["Tatah sanchintayan kuryād Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam;","Vyāpakam sarva kendram cha pratimānām pradakṣhiṇāhā. 68"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād sarvanā kendra samān ane vyāpak evā Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne sambhāratā pratimāonī pradakṣhiṇā karavī. (68)","english":"One should then perform pradakshinās of the murtis while contemplating upon Akshar- Purushottam Maharaj, who is pervasive and the focus of all. (68)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"69":{"sanskrit":["Sāṣhṭāngā daṇḍavat kāryāh praṇāmāh puruṣhais-tataha;","Nārībhis-tūpavishyaiva panchāngā dāsa-bhāvataha. 69"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād dāsbhāve puruṣhoe sāṣhṭāng danḍavat praṇām karavā ane strīoe besīne panchāng praṇām karavā. (69)","english":"Thereafter, with dāsbhāv, males should perform sāshtāng dandvat pranāms and females should sit and offer panchāng pranāms. (69)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"70":{"sanskrit":["Praṇāmo daṇḍavach-chaikah kṣhamā-yāchana-pūrvakam;","Bhakta-droha-nivārārtham kāryo’dhiko hi pratyaham. 70"],"gujarati":"Koī bhaktano droh thayo hoy tenā nivāraṇne arthe kṣhamā-yāchanā-pūrvak pratidin ek danḍavat praṇām adhik karavo. (70)","english":"One should perform an additional dandvat pranām every day to seek forgiveness for hurting or harboring ill-will towards another devotee. (70)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"71":{"sanskrit":["Divya-bhāvena bhaktyā cha tad-anu prārthayej-japan;","Swāminārāyaṇam mantram shubha-sankalpa-pūrtaye. 71"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād Swāminārāyaṇ mantrano jap karatā shubh sankalponī pūrti māṭe divyabhāv ane bhaktie sahit prārthanā (dhūn) karavī. (71)","english":"Then, to fulfil one’s noble wishes, one should pray with divyabhāv and devotion while chanting the Swaminarayan mantra (dhun). (71)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"72":{"sanskrit":["Bhaktitah pūjayitvaivam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam;","Punar-āgama-mantreṇa prasthāpayen-nijātmani. 72"],"gujarati":"Ā rīte bhakti-bhāve pūjā karīne punarāgaman mantrathī Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne potānā ātmāne viṣhe padharāvavā. (72)","english":"After devoutly performing puja in this way, one should re-install Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj within one’s ātmā by reciting the Punaragaman Mantra.¹² (72)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["12. ‘Punaragaman Mantra’ refers to the verse recited to conclude one’s puja."]},"73":{"sanskrit":["Bhaktyaiva divya-bhāvena pūjā te samanuṣhṭhitā;","Gachchhā’tha tvam mad-ātmānam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottama. 73"],"gujarati":"Punarāgaman mantra ā pramāṇe chhe:\nBhaktyaiva divy-abhāvena pūjā te sam-anuṣhṭhitā;\nGachchhātha tvam madātmānam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottama.⁴ (73)","english":"The Punaragaman Mantra is as follows:\nBhaktyaiva divya-bhāvena pujā te sam-anushthitā,\nGachchhā’tha tvam mad-ātmānam Akshara-Purushottama.¹³ (73)","gujFoot":["4. Mantra upar lakhyā pramāṇe ja bolavo. Mantrano tātparyārth ā pramāṇe chhe: He Akṣharbrahma sahit birājmān Puruṣhottam Nārāyaṇ! Āpanī pūjā bhakti-bhāvthī ane divya-bhāvthī ja me sampanna karī chhe. Have āp mārā ātmāne viṣhe virājit thāo."],"engFoot":["13. This mantra should be recited as written. The meaning of this mantra is as follows: “O Purushottam Narayan together with Aksharbrahman! I have performed your puja with devotion and divyabhāv. Now, please reside within my ātmā.”"]},"74":{"sanskrit":["Tatah satsanga-dārḍhyāya shāstram paṭhyam cha pratyaham;","Ādeshāsh-chopadeshāsh-cha yatra santi Harer guroho. 74"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād satsangnī dṛuḍhatā māṭe jemā Shrīhari tathā gurunā updesho ane ādesho samāyā hoy tevā shāstranu roj vānchan karavu. (74)","english":"To strengthen one’s satsang, one should then daily read shastras that encompass the teachings and instructions of Shri Hari and the gurus. (74)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"75":{"sanskrit":["Tad-anu praṇamed bhaktān ādarān-namra-bhāvatah;","Evam pūjām samāpyaiva kuryāt sva-vyāvahārikam. 75"],"gujarati":"Tyār bād ādar ane namrabhāve bhaktone praṇām karavā. Ā rīte pūjā karīne pachhī ja potānā vyavahārnu kārya karavu. (75)","english":"Thereafter, one should bow to devotees with reverence and humility. Only after performing puja in this way should one engage in one’s daily activities. (75)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"76":{"sanskrit":["Bhojyam naiva na peyam vā vinā pūjām jalādikam;","Pravāsa-gamane chā’pi pūjām naiva pari-tyajet. 76"],"gujarati":"Pūjā karyā vinā jamavu nahī ne pāṇī vagere paṇ na pīvu. Pravāse gayā hoīe to paṇ pūjāno tyāg na karavo. (76)","english":"One should not eat food or even drink water or other liquids without performing puja. One should not give up one’s puja even during outings. (76)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"77":{"sanskrit":["Vārdhakyena cha rogādyair anyā’paddhetunā tathā;","Pūjārtham asamarthash-chet tadā’nyaih kārayet sa tām. 77"],"gujarati":"Vṛuddhāvasthā, rogādi tathā anya āpattine līdhe pote pūjā karavā asamarth hoy teṇe anya pāse te pūjā karāvavī. (77)","english":"If one is incapable of doing puja because of old age, illness or other difficulties, one should have one’s puja performed by another. (77)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"78":{"sanskrit":["Svīyapūjā svatantrā tu sarvai rakṣhyā gṛuhe pṛuthak;","Janmano divasād eva pūjā grāhyā sva-santatehe. 78"],"gujarati":"Gharmā pratyek satsangīe potānī swatantra pūjā rākhavī. Vaḷī putra ke putrīno janma thāy te divasathī ja santān māṭe pūjā laī levī. (78)","english":"Every satsangi in a household should keep their own separate puja. Moreover, one should acquire a puja for a child on the same day that he or she is born. (78)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"79":{"sanskrit":["Bhakti-prārthana-satsanga-hetunā prati-vāsaram;","Sundaram mandiram sthāpyam sarvaih satsangibhir gṛuhe. 79"],"gujarati":"Nitya pratye bhakti, prārthanā tathā satsang māṭe sarve satsangīoe gharmā sundar mandir sthāpavu. Temā bhakti-bhāve vidhivat Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam tathā paramparāmā āvel guṇātīt guruo padharāvavā. (79-80)","english":"All satsangis should place a beautiful mandir within their homes where they can daily offer devotion, pray and practice satsang. Within the mandir, one should devoutly and ceremonially consecrate the murtis of Akshar-Purushottam and the Gunatit gurus of the tradition. (79–80)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"80":{"sanskrit":["Prasthāpyau vidhivat tasminn-Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamau;","Guravash-cha Guṇātītā bhaktyā paramparā-gatāhā. 80"],"gujarati":"Nitya pratye bhakti, prārthanā tathā satsang māṭe sarve satsangīoe gharmā sundar mandir sthāpavu. Temā bhakti-bhāve vidhivat Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam tathā paramparāmā āvel guṇātīt guruo padharāvavā. (79-80)","english":"All satsangis should place a beautiful mandir within their homes where they can daily offer devotion, pray and practice satsang. Within the mandir, one should devoutly and ceremonially consecrate the murtis of Akshar-Purushottam and the Gunatit gurus of the tradition. (79–80)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"81":{"sanskrit":["Prātah prati-dinam sāyam sarvaih satsangibhir janaihi;","Ārārtikyam vidhātavyam sa-stuti gṛuha-mandire. 81"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangī janoe prātahkāḷe tathā sānje ghar-mandirmā pratidin ārtī karavī ne sāthe stutinu gān karavu. (81)","english":"Every morning and evening, all satsangis should perform the ārti and sing the stuti before the ghar mandir. (81)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"82":{"sanskrit":["Uchchaih swarair Jaya Swāmi-nārāyaṇeti bhaktitaha;","Sa-tāli-vādanam geyam sthireṇa chetasā tadā. 82"],"gujarati":"Ārtī samaye chittane sthir karī bhaktie sahit, tālī vagāḍatā ane uchcha sware ‘Jay Swāminārāyaṇ jay Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam...’ em ārtīnu gān karavu. (82)","english":"While performing the ārti, one should devoutly sing aloud the ārti ‘Jay Swaminarayan, Jay Akshar-Purushottam…’ with a steady mind and while clapping. (82)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"83":{"sanskrit":["Yaiva rasavatī pakvā mandire tām nivedayet;","Uchchārya prārthanam bhaktyā tatah prasāditam jamet. 83"],"gujarati":"Je rasoī banāvī hoy te mandirmā dharāvavī ane prasādībhūt thayel bhojan bhakti-bhāv-pūrvak prārthanā bolīne pachhī jamavu. (83)","english":"Offer whatever food has been prepared [to the murtis] in the ghar mandir and after devoutly reciting prayers, eat the sanctified meal. (83)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"84":{"sanskrit":["Haraye’narpya na grāhyam anna-fala-jalādikam;","Shuddhau shankitam annādi nā’dyānneshe nivedayet. 84"],"gujarati":"Bhagwānne arpaṇ karyā vagar anna, faḷ ke jalādi grahaṇ na karavu. Jenī shuddhine viṣhe shankā hoy tevā annādi Bhagwānne na dharāvavā ane na jamavā. (84)","english":"One should not consume foods, fruits, water and other items without first offering them to Bhagwan. Foods and other items that may be impure should not be offered to Bhagwan nor should they be eaten. (84)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"85":{"sanskrit":["Kīrtanam vā japam kuryāt smṛutyādi vā yathā-ruchi;","Gṛuha-mandiram āsthāya bhāvatah sthira-chetasā. 85"],"gujarati":"Ghar-mandirmā besīne bhāve karīne sthir chitte kīrtan, jap ke smṛuti vagere potānī ruchi anusār karavu. (85)","english":"While sitting in front of the ghar mandir, one should, with devout feelings and concentration, sing kirtans, chant and engage in smruti or other acts of devotion according to one’s preferences. (85)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"86":{"sanskrit":["Sambhūya pratyaham kāryā gṛuha-sabhā gṛuhasthitaihi;","Kartavyam bhajanam goṣhṭhih shāstra-pāṭhādi tatra cha. 86"],"gujarati":"Gharnā sabhyoe bhegā thaī roj ghar-sabhā karavī ane temā bhajan, goṣhṭhi tathā shāstronu vānchan ityādi karavu. (86)","english":"Family members should gather daily for ghar sabhā and engage in bhajan, discussions, scriptural reading and other devotional activities. (86)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"87":{"sanskrit":["Shuddhopāsana-bhaktim hi poṣhayitum cha rakṣhitum;","Bhaktim mandira-nirmāṇa-rūpām prāvartayaddharihi. 87"],"gujarati":"Shrīharie shuddha upāsanā-bhaktinā poṣhaṇ ane rakṣhaṇ māṭe mandir nirmāṇrūp bhaktinu pravartan karyu. Ane Bhagwānnī jem ja temanā uttam bhakta evā Akṣharbrahmanī Bhagwānnī sāthe sevā karavā māṭe āgnā karī. (87-88)","english":"Shri Hari inspired the creation of mandirs as a form of devotion to foster and protect pure upāsanā and bhakti. He instructed that, along with Bhagwan, one should also serve his supreme devotee, Aksharbrahman, in the very same manner that one serves Bhagwan. (87–88)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"88":{"sanskrit":["Tathaivā’gnāpayām āsa sevārtham Hariṇā saha;","Tasya chottama-bhaktasya tasyevaivā’kṣharasya cha. 88"],"gujarati":"Shrīharie shuddha upāsanā-bhaktinā poṣhaṇ ane rakṣhaṇ māṭe mandir nirmāṇrūp bhaktinu pravartan karyu. Ane Bhagwānnī jem ja temanā uttam bhakta evā Akṣharbrahmanī Bhagwānnī sāthe sevā karavā māṭe āgnā karī. (87-88)","english":"Shri Hari inspired the creation of mandirs as a form of devotion to foster and protect pure upāsanā and bhakti. He instructed that, along with Bhagwan, one should also serve his supreme devotee, Aksharbrahman, in the very same manner that one serves Bhagwan. (87–88)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"89":{"sanskrit":["Vartata uttamo bhakto Brahma Bhagavato’kṣharam;","Nityam māyā-param nityam Hari-sevāratam yataha. 89"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahma Bhagwānnā uttam bhakta chhe, kāraṇ ke teo nitya māyāpar chhe ane nitya Bhagwānnī sevāmā ramamāṇ hoy chhe. (89)","english":"Aksharbrahman is Bhagwan’s supreme devotee because he eternally transcends māyā and is forever engrossed in Bhagwan’s service. (89)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"90":{"sanskrit":["Mandirāṇām hi nirmāṇam tad-āgnām-anusṛutya cha;","Divyānām kriyate bhaktyā sarva-kalyāṇa-hetunā. 90"],"gujarati":"Te āgnāne anusarīne sarvanu kalyāṇ thāy te hetuthī divya mandironu nirmāṇ bhakti-bhāvthī karavāmā āve chhe ane tenā madhya-khanḍmā Puruṣhottam Bhagwānnī mūrtinī sāthe Akṣharbrahmanī mūrti paṇ vidhivat sthāpavāmā āve chhe. (90-91)","english":"To fulfill this ordinance and to grant moksha all, divine mandirs are devoutly constructed and the murti of Aksharbrahman is also ceremoniously consecrated with Purushottam Bhagwan in the central shrines [of these mandirs]. (90–91)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"91":{"sanskrit":["Puruṣhottama-mūrtyā tad-madhya-khaṇḍe yathā-vidhi;","Sahitam sthāpyate mūrtir-Akṣharasyā’pi Brahmaṇaha. 91"],"gujarati":"Te āgnāne anusarīne sarvanu kalyāṇ thāy te hetuthī divya mandironu nirmāṇ bhakti-bhāvthī karavāmā āve chhe ane tenā madhya-khanḍmā Puruṣhottam Bhagwānnī mūrtinī sāthe Akṣharbrahmanī mūrti paṇ vidhivat sthāpavāmā āve chhe. (90-91)","english":"To fulfill this ordinance and to grant moksha all, divine mandirs are devoutly constructed and the murti of Aksharbrahman is also ceremoniously consecrated with Purushottam Bhagwan in the central shrines [of these mandirs]. (90–91)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"92":{"sanskrit":["Evam eva gṛuhādyeṣhu kṛuteṣhu mandireṣhvapi;","Madhye prasthāpyate nityam sā’kṣharah Puruṣhottamaha. 92"],"gujarati":"E ja rīte ghar ādi sthaḷone viṣhe karel mandiromā paṇ madhyamā hammeshā Akṣharbrahma sahit Puruṣhottam Bhagwānne prasthāpit karavāmā āve chhe. (92)","english":"Similarly, Aksharbrahman and Purushottam Bhagwan are also always consecrated in the central shrines of mandirs in homes and other places. (92)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"93":{"sanskrit":["Prātah sāyam yathā-kālam sarva-satsangibhir janaihi;","Nikaṭam mandiram gamyam bhaktyā darshāya pratyaham. 93"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangīoe savāre, sānje athavā potānā anukūḷ samaye pratidin bhaktie karīne samīpe āvel mandire darshane javu. (93)","english":"Daily, in the morning, evening or at another convenient time, all satsangis should devoutly go to a nearby mandir for darshan. (93)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"94":{"sanskrit":["Yathā sva-dharma-rakṣhā syāt tathaiva vastra-dhāraṇam;","Satsangi-nara-nārībhih karaṇīyam hi sarvadā. 94"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangī nar-nārīoe sadāy je rīte potānā dharmanī rakṣhā thāya te ja rīte vastro dhāravā. (94)","english":"All satsangi men and women should always dress in a manner that safeguards their dharma. (94)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"95":{"sanskrit":["Satsanga-dṛuḍhatārtham hi sabhārtham antike sthitam;","Gantavyam prati-saptāham mandiram vā’pi maṇḍalam. 95"],"gujarati":"Satsangnī dṛuḍhatā māṭe dar aṭhavāḍiye samīp āvel mandirmā ke manḍaḷmā sabhā bharavā javu. (95)","english":"To strengthen one’s satsang, one should attend the weekly assemblies held at a nearby mandir or center. (95)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"96":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇah sākṣhād-Akṣharādhipatir-Harihi;","Paramātmā Parabrahma Bhagavān Puruṣhottamaha. 96"],"gujarati":"Akṣharādhipati Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān sākṣhāt Paramātmā Parabrahma Puruṣhottam Hari chhe. (96)","english":"Swaminarayan Bhagwan, the sovereign of Akshar, is the manifest form of Paramatma Parabrahman Purushottam Hari. (96)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"97":{"sanskrit":["Sa ekah paramopāsya iṣhṭa-devo hi nah sadā;","Tasyaiva sarvadā bhaktih kartavyā’nanya-bhāvataha. 97"],"gujarati":"E ek ja āpaṇā sadā param upāsya iṣhṭadev chhe. Temanī ja ananya bhāve sadā bhakti karavī. (97)","english":"He alone is forever our ishtadev worthy of supreme upāsanā. One should always offer singular devotion to him only. (97)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"98":{"sanskrit":["Sākṣhād Brahmā’kṣharam Swāmī Guṇātītah sanātanam;","Tasya paramparā’dyā’pi Brahmā’kṣharasya rājate. 98"],"gujarati":"Guṇātītānand Swāmī sākṣhāt sanātan Akṣharbrahma chhe. E Akṣharbrahmanī paramparā āje paṇ virājamān chhe. (98)","english":"Gunatitanand Swami is the manifest form of the eternal Aksharbrahman. This Aksharbrahman paramparā is manifest even today. (98)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"99":{"sanskrit":["Guṇātīta-samārabdha-paramparā-pratiṣhṭhitaha;","Prakaṭā’kṣhara-brahmaikah sampradāye’sti no guruhu. 99"],"gujarati":"Sampradāymā Guṇātītānand Swāmīthī ārambhāyel guru-paramparāmā āvel pragaṭ Akṣharbrahma e ek ja āpaṇā guru chhe. (99)","english":"In the Sampraday’s tradition of gurus that began with Gunatitanand Swami, only the present form of Aksharbrahman is our guru. (99)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"100":{"sanskrit":["Eka eveṣhṭa-devo nah eka eva gurus-tathā;","Ekash-chaivā’pi siddhānta evam nah ekatā sadā. 100"],"gujarati":"Āpaṇā iṣhṭadev ek ja chhe, guru ek ja chhe ane siddhānt paṇ ek ja chhe em āpaṇī sadā ekatā chhe. (100)","english":"Our ishtadev is the same, our guru is the same and our siddhānt is also the same – thus, we are always united. (100)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"101":{"sanskrit":["Siddhāntam suvijānīyād Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam;","Brahmavidyātmakam divyam vaidikam cha sanātanam. 101"],"gujarati":"Brahma-vidyārūp, Vaidik ane sanātan evā divya Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam siddhāntne jāṇavo. (101)","english":"One should know [and realize] the divine Akshar-Purushottam siddhānt, which is Vedic, eternal and the form of brahmavidyā. (101)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"102":{"sanskrit":["Jīvas-tatheshvarash-chaiva māyā brahmā’kṣharam tathā;","Parabrahmeti tattvāni bhinnāni pancha sarvadā. 102"],"gujarati":"Jīv, īshwar, māyā, Akṣharbrahma tathā Parabrahma e pānch tattvo sadāy bhinna chhe, nitya chhe, satya chhe em mumukṣhuoe jāṇavu - em swayam Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwāne spaṣhṭa siddhānt karyo chhe. (102-103)","english":"Mumukshus should realize that the five entities – jiva, ishwar, māyā, Aksharbrahman and Parabrahman – are forever distinct, eternal and true. Swaminarayan Bhagwan himself established this clear siddhānt. (102–103)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"103":{"sanskrit":["Nityān yatha cha satyāni vigneyāni mumukṣhubhihi;","Swāminārāyaṇenaivam siddhāntitam svayam sfuṭam. 103"],"gujarati":"Jīv, īshwar, māyā, Akṣharbrahma tathā Parabrahma e pānch tattvo sadāy bhinna chhe, nitya chhe, satya chhe em mumukṣhuoe jāṇavu - em swayam Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwāne spaṣhṭa siddhānt karyo chhe. (102-103)","english":"Mumukshus should realize that the five entities – jiva, ishwar, māyā, Aksharbrahman and Parabrahman – are forever distinct, eternal and true. Swaminarayan Bhagwan himself established this clear siddhānt. (102–103)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"104":{"sanskrit":["Teṣhu māyā-parau nityam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamau;","Jīvānām-īshvarāṇām cha muktis-tad-yogato bhavet. 104"],"gujarati":"Temā Akṣhar ane Puruṣhottam e be sadāy māyāthī par chhe ane jīvo tathā īshwaronī mukti temanā yogthī thāy chhe. (104)","english":"Among these entities, Akshar and Purushottam are the two who are eternally beyond māyā. Jivas and ishwars attain moksha by associating with them. (104)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"105":{"sanskrit":["Paramātmā Parabrahma param Brahmā’kṣharāt sadā;","Brahmā’pi sevate tam cha dāsa-bhāvena sarvadā. 105"],"gujarati":"Paramātmā Parabrahma sadā Akṣharbrahmathī par chhe ane Akṣharbrahma paṇ te Paramātmānī nitya dāsbhāve sevā kare chhe. (105)","english":"Paramatma Parabrahman is forever superior to Aksharbrahman. Furthermore, even Aksharbrahman eternally serves Paramatma with dāsbhāv. (105)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"106":{"sanskrit":["Sarva-kartā cha sākārah sarvopari sadā Harihi;","Mumukṣhūṇām vimokṣhāya prakaṭo vartate sadā. 106"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān sadāy sarva-kartā, sākār, sarvoparī chhe ane mumukṣhuonī mukti māṭe hammeshā pragaṭ rahe chhe. (106)","english":"Bhagwan is eternally the all-doer, with form and supreme; he always remains manifest for the moksha of mumukshus. (106)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"107":{"sanskrit":["Brahmā’kṣhara-guru-dvārā Bhagavān prakaṭah sadā;","Sahitah sakalaishvaryaih paramā’nandam arpayan. 107"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahma-swarūp guru dvārā Bhagwān potānā sakaḷ aishvaryo sahit, paramānand arpatā thakā sadāy pragaṭ rahe chhe. (107)","english":"Through the Aksharbrahman guru, Bhagwan always remains present with all of his divinity and bestows utmost bliss. (107)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"108":{"sanskrit":["Prītih kāryā’tma-buddhish-cha Brahmā’kṣhare gurau dṛuḍhā;","Pratyakṣha-Bhagavad-bhāvāt sevyo dhyeyah sa bhaktitaha. 108"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahma gurune viṣhe dṛuḍh prīti ane ātmabuddhi karavī. Temane viṣhe pratyakṣh Bhagwānno bhāv lāvīne bhaktie karīne temanī sevā tathā dhyān karavā. (108)","english":"One should foster intense love and ātmabuddhi for the Aksharbrahman guru. Believing the guru as the manifest form of Bhagwan, one should serve him and meditate on him with devotion. (108)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"109":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇo mantro divyash-chā’laukikah shubhaha;","Japyo’yam sakalair bhaktair datto’yam Hariṇā swayam. 109"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ mantra divya, alaukik ane shubh mantra chhe. Swayam Shrīharie ā mantra āpyo chhe. Sarva bhaktoe teno jap karavo. Ā mantramā ‘Swāmi’ shabdathī Akṣharbrahmane samajavā ane ‘Nārāyaṇ’ shabdathī te Akṣharbrahmathī par evā Puruṣhottamne samajavā. (109-110)","english":"The ‘Swaminarayan’ mantra is divine, beyond this world and auspicious. Shri Hari himself bestowed this mantra. All devotees should chant it. In this mantra, understand that ‘Swami’ refers to Aksharbrahman, and ‘Narayan’ refers to Purushottam, who is superior to Aksharbrahman. (109–110)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"110":{"sanskrit":["Akṣharam Brahma vigneyam mantre Swāmīti shabdataha;","Nārāyaṇeti shabdena tat-parah Puruṣhottamaha. 110"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ mantra divya, alaukik ane shubh mantra chhe. Swayam Shrīharie ā mantra āpyo chhe. Sarva bhaktoe teno jap karavo. Ā mantramā ‘Swāmi’ shabdathī Akṣharbrahmane samajavā ane ‘Nārāyaṇ’ shabdathī te Akṣharbrahmathī par evā Puruṣhottamne samajavā. (109-110)","english":"The ‘Swaminarayan’ mantra is divine, beyond this world and auspicious. Shri Hari himself bestowed this mantra. All devotees should chant it. In this mantra, understand that ‘Swami’ refers to Aksharbrahman, and ‘Narayan’ refers to Purushottam, who is superior to Aksharbrahman. (109–110)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"111":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇeneha siddhānto’yam prabodhitaha;","Gurubhish-cha Guṇātītair digante’yam pravartitaha. 111"],"gujarati":"Ā siddhānt Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇe ā lokmā prabodhyo. Guṇātīt guruoe tenu digantmā pravartan karyu. Shāstrījī Mahārāje tene mūrtimān karyo. Guruonā jīvan-charitra-granthomā tenī punah dṛuḍhatā karāvavāmā āvī. Ā siddhāntne guruhari Pramukh Swāmī Mahārāje potānā hastākṣharthī lakhī sthir karyo. Sākṣhāt guruharinā prasangthī ā siddhānt jīvanmā prāpt karī shakāy chhe. Te ā satya sanātan muktiprad siddhāntne ja divya ‘Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Darshan’ kahevāmā āve chhe. (111-114)","english":"Bhagwan Swaminarayan revealed this siddhānt in this world. The Gunatit gurus spread it throughout the world. Shastriji Maharaj enshrined it in the form of murtis. It was reaffirmed in the jivancharitra texts of the gurus. This siddhānt was securely established by guruhari Pramukh Swami Maharaj in his own handwriting. This siddhānt may be imbibed in one’s life through the association of the manifest guruhari. It is this eternal and moksha-bestowing siddhānt that is known as the divine ‘Akshar-Purushottam Darshan’. (111–114)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"112":{"sanskrit":["Yagnapuruṣhadāsena sthāpito mūrti-mattayā;","Guru-charitra-grantheṣhu punar ayam dṛuḍhāyitaha. 112"],"gujarati":"Ā siddhānt Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇe ā lokmā prabodhyo. Guṇātīt guruoe tenu digantmā pravartan karyu. Shāstrījī Mahārāje tene mūrtimān karyo. Guruonā jīvan-charitra-granthomā tenī punah dṛuḍhatā karāvavāmā āvī. Ā siddhāntne guruhari Pramukh Swāmī Mahārāje potānā hastākṣharthī lakhī sthir karyo. Sākṣhāt guruharinā prasangthī ā siddhānt jīvanmā prāpt karī shakāy chhe. Te ā satya sanātan muktiprad siddhāntne ja divya ‘Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Darshan’ kahevāmā āve chhe. (111-114)","english":"Bhagwan Swaminarayan revealed this siddhānt in this world. The Gunatit gurus spread it throughout the world. Shastriji Maharaj enshrined it in the form of murtis. It was reaffirmed in the jivancharitra texts of the gurus. This siddhānt was securely established by guruhari Pramukh Swami Maharaj in his own handwriting. This siddhānt may be imbibed in one’s life through the association of the manifest guruhari. It is this eternal and moksha-bestowing siddhānt that is known as the divine ‘Akshar-Purushottam Darshan’. (111–114)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"113":{"sanskrit":["Pramukha-guruṇā yo’yam svīyā’kṣharaih sthirī-kṛutaha;","Sākṣhād guroh prasangena labhyate’yam hi jīvane. 113"],"gujarati":"Ā siddhānt Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇe ā lokmā prabodhyo. Guṇātīt guruoe tenu digantmā pravartan karyu. Shāstrījī Mahārāje tene mūrtimān karyo. Guruonā jīvan-charitra-granthomā tenī punah dṛuḍhatā karāvavāmā āvī. Ā siddhāntne guruhari Pramukh Swāmī Mahārāje potānā hastākṣharthī lakhī sthir karyo. Sākṣhāt guruharinā prasangthī ā siddhānt jīvanmā prāpt karī shakāy chhe. Te ā satya sanātan muktiprad siddhāntne ja divya ‘Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Darshan’ kahevāmā āve chhe. (111-114)","english":"Bhagwan Swaminarayan revealed this siddhānt in this world. The Gunatit gurus spread it throughout the world. Shastriji Maharaj enshrined it in the form of murtis. It was reaffirmed in the jivancharitra texts of the gurus. This siddhānt was securely established by guruhari Pramukh Swami Maharaj in his own handwriting. This siddhānt may be imbibed in one’s life through the association of the manifest guruhari. It is this eternal and moksha-bestowing siddhānt that is known as the divine ‘Akshar-Purushottam Darshan’. (111–114)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"114":{"sanskrit":["Ayam eva sa siddhānto mukti-pradah sanātanaha;","Uchyate darshanam divyam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam. 114"],"gujarati":"Ā siddhānt Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇe ā lokmā prabodhyo. Guṇātīt guruoe tenu digantmā pravartan karyu. Shāstrījī Mahārāje tene mūrtimān karyo. Guruonā jīvan-charitra-granthomā tenī punah dṛuḍhatā karāvavāmā āvī. Ā siddhāntne guruhari Pramukh Swāmī Mahārāje potānā hastākṣharthī lakhī sthir karyo. Sākṣhāt guruharinā prasangthī ā siddhānt jīvanmā prāpt karī shakāy chhe. Te ā satya sanātan muktiprad siddhāntne ja divya ‘Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Darshan’ kahevāmā āve chhe. (111-114)","english":"Bhagwan Swaminarayan revealed this siddhānt in this world. The Gunatit gurus spread it throughout the world. Shastriji Maharaj enshrined it in the form of murtis. It was reaffirmed in the jivancharitra texts of the gurus. This siddhānt was securely established by guruhari Pramukh Swami Maharaj in his own handwriting. This siddhānt may be imbibed in one’s life through the association of the manifest guruhari. It is this eternal and moksha-bestowing siddhānt that is known as the divine ‘Akshar-Purushottam Darshan’. (111–114)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"115":{"sanskrit":["Siddhāntam paramam divyam etādṛusham vichintayan;","Satsangam niṣhṭhayā kuryād ānandotsāha-pūrvakam. 115"],"gujarati":"Āvā param divya siddhāntnu chintavan karatā karatā niṣhṭhāthī ane ānand-utsāh-pūrvak satsang karavo. (115)","english":"While reflecting on such a supremely divine siddhānt, one should engage in satsang with conviction, joy and enthusiasm. (115)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"116":{"sanskrit":["Nijā’tmānam brahmarūpam deha-traya-vilakṣhaṇam;","Vibhāvyopāsanam kāryam sadaiva Parabrahmaṇaha. 116"],"gujarati":"Traṇ dehthī vilakṣhaṇ evā potānā ātmāne viṣhe brahmarūpnī vibhāvanā karī sadaiv Parabrahmanī upāsanā karavī. (116)","english":"Identify one’s ātmā, which is distinct from the three bodies, as brahmarup and always offer upāsanā to Parabrahman. (116)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"117":{"sanskrit":["Akṣharādhipater bhaktim sa-dharmām ācharet sadā;","Dharmeṇa rahitām naiva bhaktim kuryāt kadāchana. 117"],"gujarati":"Akṣharādhipati Paramātmānī bhakti sadā dharme sahit karavī. Kyārey dharme rahit bhakti na karavī. (117)","english":"One should offer devotion to Paramatma, the sovereign of Akshar, while always upholding dharma. One should never perform bhakti without dharma. (117)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"118":{"sanskrit":["Bhaktim vā gnānam ālambya naivā’dharmam charej-janaha;","Api parva-visheṣham vā’ lambya nā’dharmam ācharet. 118"],"gujarati":"Bhaktinu ke gnānnu ālamban laīne ke koī parvanu ālamban laīne paṇ manuṣhyae adharmanu ācharaṇ na karavu. (118)","english":"One should not behave immorally even under the pretext of devotion, wisdom or festivals. (118)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"119":{"sanskrit":["Bhangā-surādi-pānam vā dyūtādi-krīḍanam tathā;","Gāli-dānādikam naiva parvasvapi samācharet. 119"],"gujarati":"Parvane viṣhe paṇ bhāng, dārū vagerenu pān karavu, jugār vagere ramavu, gāḷo bolavī ityādi na karavu. (119)","english":"Even during festivities, one should abstain from bhang, alcohol and other such substances, as well as gambling, swearing and other such activities. (119)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"120":{"sanskrit":["Parasmād Brahmaṇo’nyasmin-nakṣharād Brahmaṇas-tathā;","Prītyabhāvo hi vairāgyam angam bhakteh sahāyakam. 120"],"gujarati":"Parabrahma tathā Akṣharbrahma sivāya anyatra prīti na hovī te vairāgya chhe. Te bhaktinu sahāyak ang chhe. (120)","english":"Vairāgya is to not have love for anything or anyone other than Parabrahman and Aksharbrahman. It serves to support bhakti. (120)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"121":{"sanskrit":["Nindā-lajjā-bhayā’padbhyah satsangam na pari-tyajet;","Swāminārāyaṇam Devam tad-bhaktim karhichid gurum. 121"],"gujarati":"Nindā, lajjā, bhay ke mushkelīone līdhe kyārey satsang, Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān, temanī bhakti ane guruno tyāg na karavo. (121)","english":"When faced with criticism, shame, fear or difficulty, one should never abandon satsang, Swaminarayan Bhagwan, devotion towards him, or the guru. (121)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"122":{"sanskrit":["Sevā Haresh-cha bhaktānām kartavyā shuddha-bhāvataha;","Mahad-bhāgyam mamāstīti matvā sva-mokṣha-hetunā. 122"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān ane bhaktonī sevā shuddhabhāve, mārā moṭā bhāgya chhe em mānīne potānā mokṣha māṭe karavī. (122)","english":"One should serve Bhagwan and his devotees with pure intentions, believing it to be one’s great fortune and with the goal of attaining one’s moksha. (122)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"123":{"sanskrit":["Neyo na vyarthatām kālah satsangam bhajanam vinā;","Ālasyam cha pramādādi pari-tyājyam hi sarvadā. 123"],"gujarati":"Satsang ane bhajan vinā vyartha kāḷ nirgamavo nahī. Āḷas tathā pramād vagereno hammeshā parityāg karavo. (123)","english":"One should not let time pass wastefully without satsang or devotion. One should always give up laziness and negligence. (123)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"124":{"sanskrit":["Kuryāddhi bhajanam kurvan kriyā āgnā’nusārataha;","Kriyā-bandhah kriyā-bhārah kriyāmānas-tato na hi. 124"],"gujarati":"Bhajan karatā karatā kriyā karavī. Āgnā anusāre karavī. Ām karavāthī kriyānu bandhan na thāy, kriyāno bhār na lāge ane kriyānu mān na āve. (124)","english":"One should perform tasks while engaging in devotion and according to āgnā. By doing so, one will not become attached to one’s actions, be burdened by them or develop ego because of them. (124)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"125":{"sanskrit":["Sevayā kathayā smṛutyā dhyānena paṭhanādibhihi;","Sufalam samayam kuryād Bhagavat-kīrtanādibhihi. 125"],"gujarati":"Sevā, kathā, smaraṇ, dhyān, paṭhanādi tathā bhagwat-kīrtan vagerethī samayne sufaḷ karavo. (125)","english":"One should fruitfully use time by performing sevā, listening to discourses, smruti, meditating, studying, singing kirtans of Bhagwan and engaging in other such activities. (125)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"126":{"sanskrit":["Sva-dur-guṇān apā-kartum sam-prāptum sad-guṇāns-tathā;","Satsangā’shrayaṇam kāryam svasya parama-muktaye. 126"],"gujarati":"Satsangno āsharo potānā durguṇone ṭāḷavā, sadguṇone prāpt karavā ane potānā param kalyāṇ māṭe karavo. (126)","english":"One should take the refuge of satsang to rid oneself of flaws, acquire virtues and attain ultimate moksha. (126)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"127":{"sanskrit":["Prasannatām samāvāptum Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho;","Guṇātīta-gurūṇām cha satsangam āshrayet sadā. 127"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān tathā guṇātīt guruonī prasannatā prāpt karavā sadā satsangno āsharo karavo. (127)","english":"One should forever take the refuge of satsang to attain the pleasure of Swaminarayan Bhagwan and the Gunatit gurus. (127)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"128":{"sanskrit":["Aho ihaiva nah prāptāv-Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamau;","Tat-prāpti-gauravān-nityam satsang-ānandam āpnuyāt. 128"],"gujarati":"Aho! Āpaṇne Akṣhar ane Puruṣhottam banne ahī ja maḷyā chhe. Temanī prāptinā kefthī satsangnā ānandne sadāy māṇavo. (128)","english":"O! We have attained both Akshar and Purushottam here [in this life]. With the joy of having attained them, one should always relish the bliss of satsang. (128)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"129":{"sanskrit":["Sevā-bhakti-kathā-dhyāna-tapo-yātrādi sādhanam;","Mānato dambhato naiva kāryam naiverṣhyayā tathā. 129"],"gujarati":"Sevā, bhakti, kathā, dhyān, tap tathā yātrā ityādi sādhan karīe te māne karīne, dambhe karīne, īrṣhyāe karīne, spardhāe karīne, dveṣhe karīne ke pachhī laukik faḷnī ichchhāthī na ja karavu. Parantu shraddhāe sahit, shuddha-bhāvthī ane Bhagwānne rājī karavānī bhāvanāthī karavu. (129-130)","english":"One should never perform sevā, devotion, discourses, meditation, austerities, pilgrimages and other endeavors out of vanity, pretense, jealousy, competition, enmity or for the attainment of worldly fruits. However, they should be performed with faith, pure intentions and the wish to please Bhagwan. (129–130)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"130":{"sanskrit":["Spardhayā dveṣhato naiva na laukika-falechchhayā;","Shraddhayā shuddha-bhāven kāryam prasannatā-dhiyā. 130"],"gujarati":"Sevā, bhakti, kathā, dhyān, tap tathā yātrā ityādi sādhan karīe te māne karīne, dambhe karīne, īrṣhyāe karīne, spardhāe karīne, dveṣhe karīne ke pachhī laukik faḷnī ichchhāthī na ja karavu. Parantu shraddhāe sahit, shuddha-bhāvthī ane Bhagwānne rājī karavānī bhāvanāthī karavu. (129-130)","english":"One should never perform sevā, devotion, discourses, meditation, austerities, pilgrimages and other endeavors out of vanity, pretense, jealousy, competition, enmity or for the attainment of worldly fruits. However, they should be performed with faith, pure intentions and the wish to please Bhagwan. (129–130)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"131":{"sanskrit":["Dṛushyo na mānuṣho bhāvo Bhagavati tathā gurau;","Māyā-parau yato divyāv-Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamau. 131"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān tathā gurune viṣhe manuṣhyabhāv na jovo. Kāraṇ ke Akṣhar ane Puruṣhottam banne māyāthī par chhe, divya chhe. (131)","english":"One should not perceive human traits in Bhagwan or the guru, since both Akshar and Purushottam are beyond māyā and divine. (131)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"132":{"sanskrit":["Vishvāsah su-dṛuḍhī-kāryo Bhagavati tathā gurau;","Nirbalatvam pari-tyājyam dhāryam dhairyam Harer balam. 132"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān tathā gurune viṣhe vishvās dṛuḍh karavo, nirbaḷtāno tyāg karavo, dhīraj rākhavī tathā Bhagwānnu baḷ rākhavu. (132)","english":"One should develop firm faith in Bhagwan and the guru, renounce feebleness, have patience and derive strength from Bhagwan. (132)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"133":{"sanskrit":["Kāryam līlā-charitrāṇām Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho;","Shravaṇam kathanam pāṭho mananam nidi-dhyāsanam. 133"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnā līlā-charitronu shravaṇ, kathan, vānchan, manan tathā nididhyāsan karavu. (133)","english":"One should listen to, recite, read, reflect upon and repeatedly recall the incidents of Swaminarayan Bhagwan. (133)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"134":{"sanskrit":["Prasangah parayā prītyā Brahmā’kṣhara-guroh sadā;","Kartavyo divya-bhāvena pratyakṣhasya mumukṣhubhihi. 134"],"gujarati":"Mumukṣhuoe pratyakṣh Akṣharbrahma guruno prasang sadā param prīti ane divyabhāvthī karavo. (134)","english":"Mumukshus should always associate with the manifest Aksharbrahman guru with supreme love and divyabhāv. (134)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"135":{"sanskrit":["Brahmā’kṣhare gurau prītir dṛuḍhaivā’sti hi sādhanam;","Brahma-sthiteh pari-prāpteh sākṣhāt-kārasya cha Prabhoho. 135"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahma-swarūp gurune viṣhe dṛuḍh prīti e ja brāhmī sthiti tathā Bhagwānnā sākṣhātkārne pāmavānu sādhan chhe. (135)","english":"Intense affection for the Aksharbrahman guru is the only means to attaining the brāhmic state and realizing Bhagwan. (135)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"136":{"sanskrit":["Brahma-guṇa-samāvāptyai Parabrahmā’nubhūtaye;","Brahma-guroh prasangānām kartavyam mananam sadā. 136"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahma gurunā guṇo ātmasāt karavā māṭe tathā Parabrahmanī anubhūti māṭe Akṣharbrahma gurunā prasangonu sadāy manan karavu. (136)","english":"To imbibe the virtues of the Aksharbrahman guru and to experience Parabrahman, one should always reflect on the incidents of the Aksharbrahman guru. (136)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"137":{"sanskrit":["Manasā karmaṇā vāchā sevyo Guruharih sadā;","Kartavyā tatra pratyakṣha-Nārāyaṇa-svarūpa-dhīhi. 137"],"gujarati":"Man-karma-vachane guruharinu sadā sevan karavu ane temane viṣhe pratyakṣh Nārāyaṇswarūpnī bhāvanā karavī. (137)","english":"One should associate with one’s guruhari through thought, word and deed and should realize him as ‘Narayanswarup’ – the manifest form of Narayan [Parabrahman]. (137)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"138":{"sanskrit":["Shṛuṇuyān-na vaden-nā’pi vārtām hīnām balena cha;","Bala-pūrṇām sadā kuryād vārtām satsangam āsthitaha. 138"],"gujarati":"Satsangīe kyārey baḷ-rahit vāt sāmbhaḷavī nahī ane karavī paṇ nahī. Hammeshā baḷ bharelī vāto karavī. (138)","english":"A satsangi should never listen to or speak discouraging words. One should always speak encouraging words. (138)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"139":{"sanskrit":["Vārtā kāryā mahimno hi Brahma-Parama-brahmaṇoho;","Tat-sambandha-vatām chā’pi sa-sneham ādarāt sadā. 139"],"gujarati":"Preme karīne tathā ādar thakī Brahma ane Parabrahmanā mahimānī tathā temanā sambandh-vāḷānā mahimānī vāto nirantar karavī. (139)","english":"With affection and reverence, one should continuously speak of the glory of Brahman and Parabrahman and the greatness of those who are associated with them. (139)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"140":{"sanskrit":["Satsangiṣhu suhṛud-bhāvo divya-bhāvas-tathaiva cha;","Akṣharabrahma-bhāvash-cha vidhātavyo mumukṣhuṇā. 140"],"gujarati":"Mumukṣhue satsangīone viṣhe suhṛudbhāv, divyabhāv tathā brahmabhāv rākhavā. (140)","english":"Mumukshus should keep suhradbhāv, divyabhāv and brahmabhāv toward satsangis. (140)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"141":{"sanskrit":["Paramātma-Parabrahma-Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho;","Brahmā’kṣhara-svarūpasya Guṇātīta-guros-tathā. 141"],"gujarati":"Paramātmā Parabrahma Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān, Akṣharbrahma-swarūp guṇātīt guru, temaṇe āpel divya siddhānt tathā temanā āshrit bhaktono viveke karīne sadāy pakṣh rākhavo. (141-142)","english":"With discretion, one should always keep the paksh of Paramatma Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan, the Aksharbrahman Gunatit guru, the divine siddhānt they have imparted and the devotees who have sought their refuge. (141–142)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"142":{"sanskrit":["Tad-arpitasya divyasya siddhāntasya cha sarvadā;","Bhaktānām tach-chhritānām cha pakṣho grāhyo vivekataha. 142"],"gujarati":"Paramātmā Parabrahma Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān, Akṣharbrahma-swarūp guṇātīt guru, temaṇe āpel divya siddhānt tathā temanā āshrit bhaktono viveke karīne sadāy pakṣh rākhavo. (141-142)","english":"With discretion, one should always keep the paksh of Paramatma Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan, the Aksharbrahman Gunatit guru, the divine siddhānt they have imparted and the devotees who have sought their refuge. (141–142)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"143":{"sanskrit":["Āgnām Bhagavato nityam Brahma-gurosh-cha pālayet;","Gnātvā tad-anuvṛuttim cha tām evā’nusared dṛuḍham. 143"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān ane brahmaswarūp gurunī āgnānu sadāy pālan karavu. Temanī anuvṛutti jāṇīne tene dṛuḍhapaṇe anusaravu. Temanī āgnā āḷas vagere mūkīne pāḷavī, tarat pāḷavī; sadā ānand, utsāh ane mahimā sāthe temane rājī karavānā bhāvthī pāḷavī. (143-144)","english":"One should always obey the commands of Bhagwan and the Brahmaswarup guru. One should realize their inner wishes and firmly abide by them. Their instructions should be followed without laziness, immediately, and always with joy, enthusiasm, mahimā and an eagerness to please them. (143–144)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"144":{"sanskrit":["Tad-āgnām pālayet sadya ālasyādi vihāya cha;","Sānandotsāha-māhātmyam tat-prasāda-dhiyā sadā. 144"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān ane brahmaswarūp gurunī āgnānu sadāy pālan karavu. Temanī anuvṛutti jāṇīne tene dṛuḍhapaṇe anusaravu. Temanī āgnā āḷas vagere mūkīne pāḷavī, tarat pāḷavī; sadā ānand, utsāh ane mahimā sāthe temane rājī karavānā bhāvthī pāḷavī. (143-144)","english":"One should always obey the commands of Bhagwan and the Brahmaswarup guru. One should realize their inner wishes and firmly abide by them. Their instructions should be followed without laziness, immediately, and always with joy, enthusiasm, mahimā and an eagerness to please them. (143–144)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"145":{"sanskrit":["Antar-dṛuṣhṭish-cha kartavyā pratyaham sthira-chetasā;","Kim kartum āgato’smīha kim kurve’ham iheti cha. 145"],"gujarati":"Pratidin sthir chitte antardṛuṣhṭi karavī ke hu ā lokmā shu karavā āvyo chhu? Ane shu karī rahyo chhu? (145)","english":"With a composed mind, one should introspect every day: “What have I come to accomplish in this world and what am I doing?” (145)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"146":{"sanskrit":["Samprāpyā’kṣhara-rūpatvam bhajeyam Puruṣhottamam;","Pratyaham chintayed evam svīya-lakṣhyam atandritaha. 146"],"gujarati":"‘Akṣharrūp thaīne hu Puruṣhottamnī bhakti karu’ em potānā lakṣhyanu chintan āḷas rākhyā vagar roj karavu. (146)","english":"“Having attained oneness with Akshar, I offer devotion to Purushottam.” In this manner, one should reflect on one’s goal each day without laziness. (146)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"147":{"sanskrit":["Kartā’yam sarva-hartā’yam sarvopari niyāmakaha;","Pratyakṣham iha labdho me Swāminārāyaṇo Harihi. 147"],"gujarati":"Ā Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān sarva-kartā-hartā chhe, sarvoparī chhe, niyāmak chhe. Teo mane ahī pratyakṣh maḷyā chhe. Āthī ja hu dhanya chhu, param bhāgyashāḷī chhu, kṛutārth chhu, nihshank chhu, nishchint chhu ane sadā sukhī chhu. (147-148)","english":"Swaminarayan Bhagwan is the all-doer,¹⁴ supreme entity and controller. I have his association here in person. For this very reason, I am joyous, greatly fortunate, fulfilled, without doubts and worries, and forever blissful. (147–148)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["14. Creator, sustainer and destroyer."]},"148":{"sanskrit":["At evā’smi dhanyo’ham parama-bhāgyavān aham;","Kṛutārthash-chaiva nihshanko nishchinto’smi sadā sukhī. 148"],"gujarati":"Ā Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān sarva-kartā-hartā chhe, sarvoparī chhe, niyāmak chhe. Teo mane ahī pratyakṣh maḷyā chhe. Āthī ja hu dhanya chhu, param bhāgyashāḷī chhu, kṛutārth chhu, nihshank chhu, nishchint chhu ane sadā sukhī chhu. (147-148)","english":"Swaminarayan Bhagwan is the all-doer,¹⁴ supreme entity and controller. I have his association here in person. For this very reason, I am joyous, greatly fortunate, fulfilled, without doubts and worries, and forever blissful. (147–148)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["14. Creator, sustainer and destroyer."]},"149":{"sanskrit":["Evam prāpter mahimnash-cha pratyaham pari-chintanam;","Prabhoh prasannatāyāsh-cha kāryam sthireṇa chetasā. 149"],"gujarati":"Ā rīte Paramātmānī divya prāptinu, mahimānu tathā temanī prasannatānu chintan dar-roj sthir chitte karavu. (149)","english":"In this way, with a composed mind, one should reflect daily on one’s divine attainment of Paramatma, his greatness and [attaining] his pleasure. (149)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"150":{"sanskrit":["Deha-traya-tryavasthāto gnātvā bhedam guṇa-trayāt;","Svātmano Brahmaṇaikatvam prati-dinam vibhāvayet. 150"],"gujarati":"Potānā ātmāne traṇ deh, traṇ avasthā tathā traṇ guṇthī judo samajī tenī Akṣharbrahma sāthe ekatānī vibhāvanā pratidin karavī. (150)","english":"Realizing one’s ātmā to be distinct from the three bodies,¹⁵ the three states,¹⁶ and the three qualities,¹⁷ one should every day believe oneself as being one with Aksharbrahman. (150)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["15. Three bodies: sthul (gross), sukshma (subtle) and kāran (causal).","16. Three states: jāgrat (waking), swapna (dream) and sushupti (deep sleep).","17. Three qualities: sattvagun, rajogun and tamogun – the three qualities of māyā."]},"151":{"sanskrit":["Pratyaham anusandheyā jagato nāsha-shīlatā;","Svātmano nityatā chintyā sach-chid-ānanda-rūpatā. 151"],"gujarati":"Dar-roj jagatnā nāshavant-paṇānu anusandhān karavu ane potānā ātmānī nityatā tathā sachchidānand-paṇānu chintavan karavu. (151)","english":"Daily, one should reflect on the impermanent nature of the world and on one’s ātmā as eternal and sachchidānand. (151)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"152":{"sanskrit":["Bhūtam yach-cha bhavad yach-cha yad-evā’gre bhaviṣhyati;","Sarvam tan me hitāyaiva Swāminārāyaṇechchhayā. 152"],"gujarati":"Je thaī gayu chhe, thaī rahyu chhe ane je kānī āgaḷ thashe te badhu ja Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnī ichchhāthī mārā hit māṭe ja chhe em mānavu. (152)","english":"One should understand that all which has happened, which is happening, and which will happen is solely due to Swaminarayan Bhagwan’s will and only for my benefit. (152)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"153":{"sanskrit":["Prārthanam pratyaham kuryād vishvāsa-bhakti-bhāvataha;","Guror Brahmaswarūpasya Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho. 153"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān tathā brahmaswarūp gurune pratidin vishvās ane bhakti-bhāvthī prārthanā karavī. (153)","english":"One should daily pray to Swaminarayan Bhagwan and the Brahmaswarup guru with faith and devotion. (153)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"154":{"sanskrit":["Mānerṣhyā-kāma-krodhādi-doṣhā’vego bhavet tadā;","Akṣharam-aham ityādi shānta-manā vichintayet. 154"],"gujarati":"Mān, īrṣhyā, kām, krodh ityādi doṣhono āveg āve tyāre ‘Hu Akṣhar chhu, Puruṣhottamno dās chhu’ em shānt mane chintavan karavu. (154)","english":"When one experiences impulses of egotism, jealousy, lust, anger, and other base instincts, one should calmly reflect: ‘I am akshar; I am a servant of Purushottam.’ (154)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"155":{"sanskrit":["Mayā saha sadaivā’sti sarva-doṣha-nivārakaha;","Swāminārāyaṇah sākṣhād evam balam cha dhārayet. 155"],"gujarati":"Ane sarva doṣhonu nivāraṇ karanārā sākṣhāt Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān sadaiv mārī sāthe chhe em baḷ rākhavu. (155)","english":"Also, one should remain strong in the belief that Swaminarayan Bhagwan himself, who is the destroyer of all base instincts, is always with me. (155)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"156":{"sanskrit":["Sva-dharmam pālayen-nityam para-dharmam pari-tyajet;","Sva-dharmo Bhagavad-gurvor āgnāyāh pari-pālanam. 156"],"gujarati":"Swadharmanu sadā pālan karavu. Par-dharmano tyāg karavo. Bhagwān ane gurunī āgnānu pālan karavu te swadharma chhe. Temanī āgnāno tyāg karī potānā mannu dhāryu karavāmā āve tene vivekī mumukṣhue par-dharma jāṇavo. (156-157)","english":"One should always observe swadharma and renounce pardharma. Swadharma means to observe the commands of Bhagwan and the guru. The wise mumukshu should realize that pardharma is disregarding their instructions and acting willfully. (156–157)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"157":{"sanskrit":["Tad-āgnām yat pari-tyajya kriyate sva-mano-dhṛutam;","Para-dharmah sa vigneyo vivekibhir mumukṣhubhihi. 157"],"gujarati":"Swadharmanu sadā pālan karavu. Par-dharmano tyāg karavo. Bhagwān ane gurunī āgnānu pālan karavu te swadharma chhe. Temanī āgnāno tyāg karī potānā mannu dhāryu karavāmā āve tene vivekī mumukṣhue par-dharma jāṇavo. (156-157)","english":"One should always observe swadharma and renounce pardharma. Swadharma means to observe the commands of Bhagwan and the guru. The wise mumukshu should realize that pardharma is disregarding their instructions and acting willfully. (156–157)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"158":{"sanskrit":["Satsanga-niyamād yaddhi viruddham dharma-lopakam;","Fala-dam api nā’charyam bhaved yad bhakti-bādhakam. 158"],"gujarati":"Je karma faḷ āpe tevu hoy tem chhatā bhaktimā bādh karatu hoy, satsangnā niyamthī viruddha hoy tathā je ācharavāthī dharmano lop thato hoy tevā karmanu ācharaṇ na karavu. (158)","english":"One should avoid even [apparently] beneficial actions that impede devotion, transgress the niyams of satsang or cause one to lapse from dharma. (158)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"159":{"sanskrit":["Ādareṇa praṇāmaish-cha madhura-vachanādibhihi;","Yatho-chitam hi sanmānyā vṛuddhā gnāna-vayo-guṇaihi. 159"],"gujarati":"Vaye karīne, gnāne karīne ke guṇe karīne je moṭā hoy temanu ādar thakī praṇām tathā madhur-vachanādike karīne yathochit sanmān karavu. (159)","english":"One should offer appropriate respect to those who are senior in age, possess greater wisdom or are more virtuous by bowing reverently, using polite speech and expressing other forms of regard. (159)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"160":{"sanskrit":["Sadaivā’daraṇīyā hi vidvad-variṣhṭha-shikṣhakāhā;","Yathā-shakti cha sat-kāryāh sādhu-vādādi-karmaṇā. 160"],"gujarati":"Vidvāno, vaḍīlo tathā adhyāpakone sadā ādar āpavo. Sārā vachan ādi kriyāo dvārā potānī shakti pramāṇe temano satkār karavo. (160)","english":"One should always respect the learned, seniors and teachers. According to one’s capacity, one should honor them with good words and other such deeds. (160)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"161":{"sanskrit":["Jana-sambodhanam kuryād yathā-kārya-guṇādikam;","Samvardhayet tad-utsāham yathā-shakti su-karmasu. 161"],"gujarati":"Vyaktinā guṇ tathā kārya ādine anusāre tenu sambodhan karavu. Yathāshakti tene sārā kāryomā protsāhan āpavu. (161)","english":"One should address each individual according to their virtues, achievements and other merits. One should encourage them in noble works according to their abilities. (161)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"162":{"sanskrit":["Satyām vaded hitām chaiva vaded vāṇīm priyām tathā;","Mithyā’ropyo’pavādo na kasminsh-chit karhichij-jane. 162"],"gujarati":"Satya, hit ane priya vāṇī bolavī. Koī manuṣhyanī upar kyārey mithyā apavādnu āropaṇ na karavu. (162)","english":"One should speak words which are true, beneficial and loving. One should never falsely accuse any individual. (162)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"163":{"sanskrit":["Na vadet kutsitām vācham apa-shabda-kalankitām;","Shrotṛu-dukha-karīm nindyām kaṭhorām dveṣha-garbhiṇīm. 163"],"gujarati":"Apshabdothī yukta, sāmbhaḷnārne dukh kare tevī, nindya, kaṭhor ane dveṣh bharelī kutsit vāṇī na bolavī. (163)","english":"One should never utter unpleasant speech that is offensive, hurts its listener and is defamatory, harsh or hateful. (163)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"164":{"sanskrit":["Asatyam na vadet kvāpi vadet satyam hitā’vaham;","Satyam api vaden-naiva yat syād anyā’hitā’vaham. 164"],"gujarati":"Asatya kyārey na bolavu. Hit kare tevu satya bolavu. Anyanu ahit kare tevu satya paṇ na bolavu. (164)","english":"One should never speak untruth. One should express truth that is beneficial, but not utter even truth that may harm others. (164)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"165":{"sanskrit":["Anyā’vaguṇa-doṣhādi-vārtām kadā’pi nochcharet;","Tathā kṛute tvashāntih syād aprītish-cha Harer guroho. 165"],"gujarati":"Kyārey koīnā avaguṇ ke doṣhnī vāt na karavī. Em karavāthī ashānti thāy ane Bhagwān tathā guruno kurājīpo thāy. (165)","english":"One should never speak of another’s drawbacks or flaws. Doing so causes unrest and results in the displeasure of Bhagwan and the guru. (165)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"166":{"sanskrit":["Atyantā’vashyake nūnam pari-shuddhena bhāvataha;","Satya-proktau na doṣhah syād adhikāra-vatām puraha. 166"],"gujarati":"Atyant āvashyak hoy to parishuddha bhāvanāthī adhikṛut vyaktine satya kahevāmā doṣh nathī. (166)","english":"If extremely necessary, it is acceptable to convey the truth with pure intent to an authorized person. (166)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"167":{"sanskrit":["Āchāro vā vichāro vā tādṛuk kāryo na karhichit;","Anyeṣhām ahitam dukham yena syāt klesha-vardhanam. 167"],"gujarati":"Jeṇe karīne anyanu ahit thāy, tene dukh thāy ke klesh vadhe tevā āchār ke vichār kyārey na karavā. (167)","english":"One should never act or think in a way that is hurtful or damaging to others or that increases conflict. (167)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"168":{"sanskrit":["Suhṛud-bhāvena bhaktānām shubha-guṇa-gaṇān smaret;","Na grāhyo’vaguṇas-teṣhām drohah kāryo na sarvathā. 168"],"gujarati":"Suhṛudaybhāv rākhī bhaktonā shubh guṇone sambhāravā. Temano avaguṇ na levo ane koī rīte droh na karavo. (168)","english":"With suhradaybhāv, recollect the virtues of devotees. One should never view their flaws or offend them in any way. (168)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"169":{"sanskrit":["Sukhe noch-chhṛunkhalo bhūyād dukhe nodvegam āpnuyāt;","Swāminārāyaṇechchhātah sarvam pravartate yataha. 169"],"gujarati":"Sukhmā chhakī na javu ane dukhmā udveg na pāmavo. Kāraṇ ke badhu Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnī ichchhāthī pravarte chhe. (169)","english":"In happy times do not get carried away and in unhappy times do not become discouraged, since everything occurs by Swaminarayan Bhagwan’s wish. (169)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"170":{"sanskrit":["Vivādah kalaho vā’pi naiva kāryah kadāchana;","Vartitavyam vivekena rakṣhyā shāntish-cha sarvadā. 170"],"gujarati":"Kyārey paṇ koīnī sāthe vivād ke kalah na ja karavo. Hammeshā vivekthī vartavu ane shānti rākhavī. (170)","english":"One should never argue or quarrel with anyone. One should always be well-mannered and remain calm. (170)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"171":{"sanskrit":["Vachane vartane kvāpi vichāre lekhane tathā;","Kaṭhoratām bhajen-naiva janah ko’pi kadāchana. 171"],"gujarati":"Koī paṇ manuṣhye potānā vachan, vartan, vichār tathā lakhāṇmā kaṭhortā kyārey na rākhavī. (171)","english":"One should never be harsh in speech, action, thought or writing. (171)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"172":{"sanskrit":["Sevām mātuh pituh kuryād gṛuhī satsangam āshritaha;","Prati-dinam namaskāram tat-pādeṣhu nivedayet. 172"],"gujarati":"Gṛuhasth satsangīe mātā-pitānī sevā karavī. Pratidin temanā charaṇomā namaskār karavā. (172)","english":"Householder satsangis should serve their mother and father. They should bow to their feet every day. (172)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"173":{"sanskrit":["Shvashurah pitṛuvat sevyo vadhvā shvashrūsh-cha mātṛuvat;","Sva-putrīvat snuṣhā pālyā shvashrvā’pi shvashureṇa cha. 173"],"gujarati":"Vahue sasarānī sevā pitātulya gaṇī ane sāsunī sevā mātātulya gaṇī karavī. Sāsu-sasarāe paṇ putra-vadhūnu potānī putrīnī jem pālan karavu. (173)","english":"A wife should serve her father-in-law as her own father and mother-in-law as her own mother. A father- and mother-in-law should care for their daughter-in-law as they would for their own daughter. (173)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"174":{"sanskrit":["Sampālyāh putra-putryash-cha satsanga-shikṣhaṇādinā;","Anye sambandhinah sevyā yathā-shakti cha bhāvataha. 174"],"gujarati":"Gṛuhasthoe dīkarā-dīkarīonu satsang, shikṣhaṇ vagerethī sārī rīte poṣhaṇ karavu. Anya sambandhīonī potānī shakti pramāṇe bhāvthī sevā karavī. (174)","english":"Householders should diligently nurture their sons and daughters through satsang, education and other activities. They should affectionately care for their other relatives according to their means. (174)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"175":{"sanskrit":["Gṛuhe hi madhurām vāṇīm vaded vācham tyajet kaṭum;","Kam api pīḍitam naiva prakuryād malinā’shayāt. 175"],"gujarati":"Gharmā madhur vāṇī bolavī. Kaḍavī vāṇīno tyāg karavo ane malin āshaythī koīne pīḍā na pahonchāḍavī. (175)","english":"One should speak pleasantly at home. One should renounce bitter speech and not harm others with malicious intent. (175)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"176":{"sanskrit":["Militvā bhojanam kāryam gṛuhasthaih sva-gṛuhe mudā;","Atithir hi yathā-shakti sambhāvya āgato gṛuham. 176"],"gujarati":"Gṛuhasthoe potānā gharmā bhegā maḷī ānande bhojan karavu ane ghare padhārelā atithinī potānī shakti pramāṇe sambhāvanā karavī. (176)","english":"Householders should joyously eat meals together at home and provide hospitality to guests according to their means. (176)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"177":{"sanskrit":["Maraṇādi-prasangeṣhu kathā-bhajana-kīrtanam;","Kāryam visheṣhatah smāryo hyakṣhara-Puruṣhottamah. 177"],"gujarati":"Maraṇ ādi prasangomā visheṣh bhajan-kīrtan karavu, kathā karavī, Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājnu smaraṇ karavu. (177)","english":"In the event of a death or other sad occasions, one should perform additional acts of devotion, sing kirtans, engage in discourses and remember Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj. (177)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"178":{"sanskrit":["Putrī-putrātmikā svasya sanskāryā santatih sadā;","Satsanga-divya-siddhāntaih sad-āchāraish-cha sadguṇaihi. 178"],"gujarati":"Dīkarī ke dīkarā evā potānā santānone satsangnā divya siddhānto, sārā ācharaṇo ane sadguṇo vaḍe sadā sanskār āpavā. (178)","english":"One should always impart sanskārs to one’s sons and daughters by teaching them the divine principles of satsang, good conduct and virtues. (178)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"179":{"sanskrit":["Satsanga-shāstra-pāṭhādyair-garbha-sthām eva santatim;","Sanskuryāt pūrayen-niṣhṭhām Akṣhara-Puruṣhottame. 179"],"gujarati":"Santān jyāre garbhamā hoy tyārthī ja tene satsang sambandhī shāstronu vānchan vagere karīne sanskār āpavā ane Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne viṣhe niṣhṭhā pūravī. (179)","english":"From when a child is in the womb, one should instill sanskārs and conviction in Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj by reading the sacred texts of satsang and through other [noble] acts. (179)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"180":{"sanskrit":["Kudṛuṣhṭyā puruṣhair naiva striyo dṛushyāh kadāchana;","Evam eva kudṛuṣhṭyā cha strībhir dṛushyā na pūruṣhāhā. 180"],"gujarati":"Puruṣho kyārey kudṛuṣhṭie karīne strīone na jue. Te ja rīte strīo paṇ kudṛuṣhṭie karīne puruṣhone na jue. (180)","english":"Men should never look at women with a wrong intent. In the same manner, women should also never look at men with a wrong intent. (180)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"181":{"sanskrit":["Svīya-patnītarābhis-tu rahasi vasanam saha;","Āpat-kālam vinā kvāpi na kuryur gṛuhiṇo narāhā. 181"],"gujarati":"Gṛuhasthāshrammā rahyā evā puruṣhoe potānī patnī sivāya anya strīo sāthe āpatkāḷ vinā kyāy paṇ ekāntmā na rahevu. (181)","english":"Except in emergency situations, married men should never remain alone anywhere with women other than their wife. (181)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"182":{"sanskrit":["Tathaiva nahi nāryo’pi tiṣhṭheyuh sva-patītaraihi;","Puruṣhaih sākam-ekānte hyāpatti-samayam vinā. 182"],"gujarati":"Te ja rīte strīoe paṇ potānā pati sivāy anya puruṣho sāthe āpatkāḷ vinā ekāntmā na rahevu. (182)","english":"Similarly, [married] women should never remain alone with men other than their husband, except in emergency situations. (182)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"183":{"sanskrit":["Narah samīpa-sambandha-hīnām striyam spṛushen-na hi;","Naiva spṛushet tathā nārī tādṛusham puruṣhāntaram. 183"],"gujarati":"Puruṣhe samīp sambandh vinānī strīno sparsh na karavo. Te ja rīte strīe potāne samīp sambandh vinānā anya puruṣhno sparsh na karavo. (183)","english":"A male should not touch a female who is not closely related; however, he may respectfully touch one who is closely related. Similarly, a female should not touch a male who is not closely related; however, she may respectfully touch one who is closely related. (183)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"184":{"sanskrit":["Āpat-kāle’nya-rakṣhārtham sparshe doṣho na vidyate;","Anyathā niyamāh pālyā anāpattau tu sarvadā. 184"],"gujarati":"Āpatkāḷ prāpt thatā anyanī rakṣhā māṭe sparsh karavāmā doṣh nathī. Parantu jo āpatkāḷ na hoy to sadāy niyamonu pālan karavu. (184)","english":"In emergency situations, it is not a fault to touch others to protect or save them. However, if there is no emergency, then always obey the niyams. (184)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"185":{"sanskrit":["Ashlīlam yatra dṛushyam syād dharma-sanskāra-nāshakam;","Nāṭaka-chala-chitrādi tan-na pashyet kadāchana. 185"],"gujarati":"Dharma ane sanskārono nāsh kare evā ashlīl dṛushyo jemā āvatā hoy tevā nāṭako ke chal-chitro vagere kyārey na jovā. (185)","english":"One should never view dramas, films or other media that contain obscene scenes which destroy one’s dharma and sanskārs. (185)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"186":{"sanskrit":["Manuṣhyo vyasanī yah syād nirlajjo vyabhichāravān;","Tasya sango na kartavyah satsangam-āshritair-janaihi. 186"],"gujarati":"Satsangī-janoe je manuṣhya vyasanī, nirlajja tathā vyabhichārī hoy teno sang na karavo. (186)","english":"Satsangis should not associate with people who have addictions, are shameless or are adulterous. (186)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"187":{"sanskrit":["Sangash-chāritrya-hīnāyāh karaṇīyo nahi striyāhā;","Strībhihi sva-dharma-rakṣhārtham pālyāsh-cha niyamā dṛuḍham. 187"],"gujarati":"Strīoe potānā dharmanī rakṣhā māṭe chāritryahīn strīno sang na karavo ane dṛuḍhpaṇe niyamonu pālan karavu. (187)","english":"To protect one’s dharma, female devotees should not associate with immoral women and should firmly abide by the niyams. (187)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"188":{"sanskrit":["Na tādṛuk-chhṛuṇuyād vācham gītam grantham paṭhenna cha;","Pashyen-na tādṛusham dṛushyam yasmāt kāma-vivardhanam. 188"],"gujarati":"Jeṇe karīne kām-vāsanā vṛuddhi pāme tevī vāto ke gīto na sāmbhaḷavā, pustako na vānchavā tathā tevā dṛushyo na jovā. (188)","english":"One should not listen to talks or songs, read books or view scenes that increase one’s lustful desires. (188)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"189":{"sanskrit":["Dhana-dravya-dharādīnām sadā’dāna-pradānayoho;","Niyamā lekha-sākṣhyādeh pālanīyā avashyataha. 189"],"gujarati":"Dhan, dravya tathā jamīn ādinā leṇ-deṇmā hammeshā likhit karavu, sākṣhīe sahit karavu ityādi niyamo avashyapaṇe pāḷavā. (189)","english":"Transactions of wealth, possessions, land and other assets should always be conducted in writing, in the presence of a witness and by definitely following other such niyams. (189)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"190":{"sanskrit":["Prasange vyavahārasya sambandhibhir api svakaihi;","Lekhādi-niyamāh pālyāh sakalair āshritair janaihi. 190"],"gujarati":"Sarva āshrit janoe potānā sambandhīo sāthe paṇ vyavahār prasange likhit karavu ityādi niyamo pāḷavā. (190)","english":"All devotees should conduct their social dealings with even their relatives in writing and by following other such niyams. (190)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"191":{"sanskrit":["Na kāryo vyavahārash-cha duṣhṭair janaih saha kvachit;","Dīna-janeṣhu bhāvyam cha satsangibhir dayā’nvitaihi. 191"],"gujarati":"Satsangīoe kyārey durjan sāthe vyavahār na karavo ane dīn-janne viṣhe dayāvān thavu. (191)","english":"Satsangis should never engage in dealings with immoral persons and should be compassionate towards those who are meek and disadvantaged. (191)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"192":{"sanskrit":["Laukikam tvavichāryaiva sahasā karma nā’charet;","Falādikam vichāryaiva vivekena tad ācharet. 192"],"gujarati":"Laukik kārya kyārey vichāryā vagar tatkāḷ na karavu parantu faḷ vagereno vichār karīne vivek-pūrvak karavu. (192)","english":"Worldly deeds should never be performed in haste without due deliberation. They should, however, be performed with due judgment, after reflecting on their consequences and other such considerations. (192)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"193":{"sanskrit":["Lunchā kadāpi na grāhyā kaishchid api janair iha;","Naiva kāryo vyayo vyarthah kāryah svā’yā’nusārataha. 193"],"gujarati":"Koī paṇ manuṣhye kyārey lānch na levī. Dhanno vyarth vyay na karavo. Potānī āvakne anusāre dhanno vyay karavo. (193)","english":"No one should ever accept bribes. Wealth should not be spent wastefully. One should spend according to one’s income. (193)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"194":{"sanskrit":["Kartavyam lekhanam samyak svasyā’yasya vyayasya cha;","Niyamān anusṛutyaiva prashāsana-kṛutān sadā. 194"],"gujarati":"Prashāsannā niyamone anusarī hammeshā potānā āvak ane kharchanī nondh vyavasthit karavī. (194)","english":"One should always accurately keep accounts of one’s income and expenditure in accordance with government laws. (194)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"195":{"sanskrit":["Svā’yāddhi dashamo bhāgo vinsho’thavā sva-shaktitaha;","Arpyah sevā-prasādārtham Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho. 195"],"gujarati":"Potāne prāpt thatī āvakmāthī potānī shakti pramāṇe dashmo ke vīshmo bhāg Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnī sevā-prasannatā māṭe arpaṇ karavo. (195)","english":"According to one’s means, one should give one-tenth or one-twentieth of one’s income in Swaminarayan Bhagwan’s service and to attain his blessings. (195)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"196":{"sanskrit":["Svopayogā’nusāreṇa prakuryāt sangraham gṛuhī;","Anna-dravya-dhanādīnām kāla-shaktyanusārataha. 196"],"gujarati":"Gṛuhasth potānā upyogne anusāre tathā samay-shakti anusār anāj, dravya ke dhanādino sangrah kare. (196)","english":"Householders should save provisions, money and other possessions according to their needs, circumstances and means. (196)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"197":{"sanskrit":["Anna-falādibhish-chaiva yathā-shakti jalādibhihi;","Pālitāh pashu-pakṣhyādyāh sambhāvyā hi yathochitam. 197"],"gujarati":"Pāḷelā pashu-pakṣhī vagerenī anna, faḷ, jaḷ ityādi vaḍe yathāshakti uchit sambhāvanā karavī. (197)","english":"According to one’s means, one should provide suitable food, fruits, water and other sustenance for one’s domesticated animals and birds. (197)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"198":{"sanskrit":["Dhana-dravya-dharādīnām pradānā’dānayoh punaha;","Vishvāsa-hananam naiva kāryam na kapaṭam tathā. 198"],"gujarati":"Dhan, dravya ke bhūmi vagerenī leṇ-deṇmā vishvāsghāt tathā kapaṭ na karavā. (198)","english":"One should not betray the trust of or deceive others in transactions involving wealth, objects, land or other commodities. (198)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"199":{"sanskrit":["Pradātum karma-kāribhyah pratignātam dhanādikam;","Yathā-vācham pradeyam tat nonam deyam kadāchana. 199"],"gujarati":"Karmachārīone jeṭalu dhan ādi āpavānu vachan āpyu hoy te vachan pramāṇe te dhan ādi āpavu paṇ kyārey ochhu na āpavu. (199)","english":"One should pay employees the amount of money or other forms of remuneration agreed upon, but should never give less. (199)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"200":{"sanskrit":["Naiva vishvāsa-ghātam hi kuryāt satsangam āshritaha;","Pālayed vachanam dattam pratignātam na langhayet. 200"],"gujarati":"Satsangīe vishvāsghāt na karavo. Āpelu vachan pāḷavu. Pratignānu ullanghan na karavu. (200)","english":"A satsangi should not commit betrayal. One should uphold one’s promise. A pledge should not be broken. (200)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"201":{"sanskrit":["Prashāstā pālayed dharmān-niyatā ye sushāsane;","Lokānām bharaṇam puṣhṭim kuryāt sanskāra-rakṣhaṇam. 201"],"gujarati":"Sushāsan māṭe avashyapaṇe joīe te dharmone prashāsake pāḷavā. Lokonu bharaṇ-poṣhaṇ karavu. Sanskāronī rakṣhā karavī. Sarveno abhyuday thāy te māṭe swāsthya, shikṣhaṇ, sanrakṣhaṇ, vījaḷī, anāj, jaḷ vagere dvārā sārī rīte vyavasthā karavī. (201-202)","english":"Rulers should follow dharma that is necessary to govern well. They should provide for the people, foster their growth and safeguard sanskārs. They should suitably arrange services for health, education, defense, electricity, food, water and other resources for the benefit of all. (201–202)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"202":{"sanskrit":["Svāsthya-shikṣhaṇa-samrakṣhā-vidyud-anna-jalādikaihi;","Su-vyavasthā vidhātavyā sarvā’bhyudaya-hetunā. 202"],"gujarati":"Sushāsan māṭe avashyapaṇe joīe te dharmone prashāsake pāḷavā. Lokonu bharaṇ-poṣhaṇ karavu. Sanskāronī rakṣhā karavī. Sarveno abhyuday thāy te māṭe swāsthya, shikṣhaṇ, sanrakṣhaṇ, vījaḷī, anāj, jaḷ vagere dvārā sārī rīte vyavasthā karavī. (201-202)","english":"Rulers should follow dharma that is necessary to govern well. They should provide for the people, foster their growth and safeguard sanskārs. They should suitably arrange services for health, education, defense, electricity, food, water and other resources for the benefit of all. (201–202)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"203":{"sanskrit":["Guṇa-sāmarthya-ruchyādi viditvaiva janasya tu;","Tad-uchiteṣhu kāryeṣhu yojanīyo vichārya saha. 203"],"gujarati":"Koī paṇ manuṣhyanā guṇ, sāmarthya, ruchi vagere jāṇīne; vichār karī tenā māṭe uchit evā kāryomā tene joḍavo. (203)","english":"A person should be assigned suitable tasks after knowing and considering their qualities, abilities, inclinations and other such factors. (203)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"204":{"sanskrit":["Shakyā Bhagavato yatra bhaktih sva-dharma-pālanam;","Tasmin deshe nivāso hi karaṇīyah sukhena cha. 204"],"gujarati":"Je deshne viṣhe Bhagwānnī bhakti thaī shake tathā potānā dharmanu pālan thaī shake tevā deshne viṣhe sukhe nivās karavo. (204)","english":"One should happily reside in a country where one can worship Bhagwan and observe one’s dharma. (204)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"205":{"sanskrit":["Vidyā-dhanādikam prāptum deshāntaram gate’pi cha;","Satsangam ādarāt tatra kuryān-niyama-pālanam. 205"],"gujarati":"Vidyā, dhan ādinī prāpti māṭe deshāntarmā jāy tyāre tyā paṇ ādarthī satsang karavo ane niyamonu pālan karavu. (205)","english":"A person who migrates elsewhere for educational, economic or other gains should continue to reverently practice satsang and observe niyams. (205)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"206":{"sanskrit":["Yad-deshe hi sva-vāsah syāt tad-desha-niyamāsh-cha ye;","Sarvathā pālanīyāste tat-prashāsana-sammatāhā. 206"],"gujarati":"Je deshmā pote rahetā hoy te deshnā prashāsanne sammat niyamonu sarva rīte pālan karavu. (206)","english":"In the country one resides, one should observe the prescribed laws of that country in every way. (206)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"207":{"sanskrit":["Sanjāte desha-kālāder-vaiparītye tu dhairyataha;","Antar-bhajeta sānandam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam. 207"],"gujarati":"Jyāre desh-kāḷādinu viparītpaṇu thaī āve tyāre dhīraj rākhī Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājnu ānand sāthe antarmā bhajan karavu. (207)","english":"During adverse times, one should keep patience and joyously worship Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj within. (207)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"208":{"sanskrit":["Āpat-kāle tu samprāpte svīya-vāsa-sthale tadā;","Tam desham hi pari-tyajya stheyam deshāntare sukham. 208"],"gujarati":"Pote je sthānmā rahetā hoy te sthaḷe āpatkāḷ āvī paḍe tyāre te deshno tyāg karī anya deshne viṣhe sukhe nivās karavo. (208)","english":"If unfavorable circumstances arise where one lives, one should leave that place and live happily elsewhere. (208)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"209":{"sanskrit":["Kāryam bālaish-cha bālābhir bālyād vidyā’bhi-prāpaṇam;","Durāchārah kusangash-cha tyājyāni vyasanāni cha. 209"],"gujarati":"Nānā bāḷako tathā bālikāoe bāḷpaṇthī ja vidyā prāpt karavī. Durāchār, kusang ane vyasanono tyāg karavo. (209)","english":"Young boys and girls should acquire education from childhood. They should avoid inappropriate behaviour, bad company and addictions. (209)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"210":{"sanskrit":["Utsāhād ādarāt kuryāt svā’bhyāsam sthira-chetasā;","Vyarthatām na nayet kālam vidyārthī vyartha-karmasu. 210"],"gujarati":"Vidyārthīe potāno abhyās sthir chitte, utsāhthī ane ādar thakī karavo. Samayne vyarth karmomā bagāḍavo nahī. (210)","english":"Students should study with concentration, enthusiasm and respect. They should not waste their time in useless activities. (210)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"211":{"sanskrit":["Bālyād eva dṛuḍhī-kuryāt sevā-vinamratādikam;","Nirbalatām bhayam chā’pi naiva gachchhet kadāchana. 211"],"gujarati":"Bāḷpaṇthī ja sevā, vinamratā vagere dṛuḍh karavā. Kyārey nirbaḷ na thavu ane bhay na pāmavo. (211)","english":"From childhood, one should strengthen the virtues of sevā, humility and other virtues. One should never lose courage or be fearful. (211)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"212":{"sanskrit":["Bālyād eva hi satsangam kuryād bhaktim cha prārthanām;","Kāryā prati-dinam pūjā pitroh panchānga-vandanā. 212"],"gujarati":"Bāḷpaṇthī ja satsang, bhakti ane prārthanā karavā. Pratidin pūjā karavī tathā mātā-pitāne panchāng praṇām karavā. (212)","english":"From childhood, one should practice satsang, offer devotion and pray. One should daily perform puja and offer panchāng pranāms to one’s mother and father. (212)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"213":{"sanskrit":["Visheṣha-saiyamah pālyah kaumārye yauvane tathā;","Ayogya-sparsha-dṛushyādyās-tyājyāh shakti-vināshakāhā. 213"],"gujarati":"Kumār tathā yuvān avasthāmā visheṣh sanyam pāḷavo. Shaktino nāsh kare evā ayogya sparsh, dṛushya vagereno tyāg karavo. (213)","english":"During adolescence and early adulthood, one should exercise greater self-control and refrain from improper physical contact, sights and other activities that destroy one’s energies [physical, mental and spiritual]. (213)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"214":{"sanskrit":["Sat-falonnāyakam kuryād uchitam eva sāhasam;","Na kuryāt kevalam yaddhi sva-mano-loka-ranjakam. 214"],"gujarati":"Sārā faḷne āpe tevu, unnati kare tevu ane uchit hoy tevu ja sāhas karavu. Je kevaḷ potānā mannu ane lokonu ranjan kare tevu sāhas na karavu. (214)","english":"One should only undertake ventures that are appropriate and lead to good outcomes and development. However, one should not engage in ventures that merely entertain one’s mind or gratify others. (214)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"215":{"sanskrit":["Niyatodyama-kartavye nā’lasyam āpnuyāt kvachit;","Shraddhām prītim Harau kuryāt pūjām satsangam anvaham. 215"],"gujarati":"Potāne avashya karavānā udyamne viṣhe kyārey āḷas na karavī. Bhagwānne viṣhe shraddhā ane prīti karavī. Pratidin pūjā karavī ane satsang karavo. (215)","english":"One should never be lazy in undertaking one’s important tasks. One should have faith in and love towards Bhagwan. One should daily perform puja and do satsang. (215)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"216":{"sanskrit":["Sango’tra balavānl-loke yathā-sangam hi jīvanam;","Satām sangam atah kuryāt kusangam sarvathā tyajet. 216"],"gujarati":"Ā lokmā sang baḷavān chhe. Jevo sang hoy tevu jīvan bane. Āthī sārā manuṣhyono sang karavo. Kusangno sarvathā tyāg karavo. (216)","english":"In this world, the company one keeps has great influence. The type of association molds one’s life accordingly. Therefore, one should always keep the company of virtuous people and totally shun bad company. (216)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"217":{"sanskrit":["Kāmā’sakto bhaved yo hi kṛutaghno loka-vanchakaha;","Pākhaṇḍī kapaṭī yash-cha tasya sangam pari-tyajet. 217"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya kāmāsakta, kṛutaghnī, lokone chhetarnār, pākhanḍī tathā kapaṭī hoy teno sang tyajavo. (217)","english":"One should renounce the company of those who are lustful, ungrateful, dishonest, hypocritical or deceitful. (217)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"218":{"sanskrit":["Hares-tad-avatārāṇām khaṇḍanam vidadhāti yaha;","Upāsteh khaṇḍanam yash-cha kurute Paramātmanaha. 218"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya Bhagwān ane temanā avatāronu khanḍan karato hoy, Paramātmānī upāsanānu khanḍan karato hoy ane sākār Bhagwānne nirākār mānato hoy teno sang na karavo. Tevā grantho na vānchavā. (218-219)","english":"One should not associate with those who deny Bhagwan and his incarnations, disapprove of upāsanā to Paramatma or believe Bhagwan, who eternally possesses a form, to be formless. Do not read such texts. (218–219)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"219":{"sanskrit":["Sākṛutikam Parabrahma manute yo nirākṛuti;","Tasya sango na kartavyas-tādṛug-granthān paṭhen-na hi. 219"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya Bhagwān ane temanā avatāronu khanḍan karato hoy, Paramātmānī upāsanānu khanḍan karato hoy ane sākār Bhagwānne nirākār mānato hoy teno sang na karavo. Tevā grantho na vānchavā. (218-219)","english":"One should not associate with those who deny Bhagwan and his incarnations, disapprove of upāsanā to Paramatma or believe Bhagwan, who eternally possesses a form, to be formless. Do not read such texts. (218–219)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"220":{"sanskrit":["Khaṇḍanam mandirāṇām yo mūrtīnām kurute Harehe;","Satyā’hinsādi-dharmāṇām tasya sangam pari-tyajet. 220"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya mandir ane Bhagwānnī mūrtionu khanḍan karato hoy, satya-ahinsā ādi dharmonu khanḍan karato hoy tenā sangno tyāg karavo. (220)","english":"One should renounce the company of those who decry mandirs and Bhagwan’s murtis or denounce truth, non-violence and other such righteous conduct. (220)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"221":{"sanskrit":["Gurvāshraya-virodhī yo vaidika-shāstra-khaṇḍakaha;","Bhakti-mārga-virodhī syāt tasya sangam na chā’charet. 221"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya guru-sharaṇāgatino virodh karato hoy, Vaidik shāstronu khanḍan karato hoy, bhakti-mārgno virodh karato hoy teno sang na karavo. (221)","english":"One should not associate with those who oppose taking refuge in a guru, Vedic texts or the path of bhakti. (221)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"222":{"sanskrit":["Buddhimān api loke syād vyāvahārika-karmasu;","Na sevyo bhakti-hīnash-chech-chhāstra-pārangato’pi vā. 222"],"gujarati":"Koī manuṣhya lokmā vyāvahārik kāryomā buddhivāḷo hoy athavā shāstromā pārangat paṇ hoy, tem chhatā paṇ jo te bhaktie rahit hoy to teno sang na karavo. (222)","english":"One should avoid the company of a person who is devoid of devotion, even if such a person is intelligent in worldly activities or learned in the shastras. (222)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"223":{"sanskrit":["Shraddhām eva tiras kṛutya hyādhyātmikeṣhu kevalam;","Puras-karoti yas-tarkam tat-sangam-ācharen-na hi. 223"],"gujarati":"Ādhyātmik viṣhayomā shraddhāno ja tiraskār karī je manuṣhya kevaḷ tarkane ja āgaḷ karato hoy teno sang na karavo. (223)","english":"One should not associate with those who ridicule faith in spiritual matters and promote logic alone. (223)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"224":{"sanskrit":["Satsange’pi kusango yo gneyah so’pi mumukṣhubhihi;","Tat-sangash-cha na kartavyo haribhaktaih kadāchana. 224"],"gujarati":"Mumukṣhu haribhaktoe satsangmā rahel kusangne paṇ jāṇavo ane kyārey teno sang na karavo. (224)","english":"Mumukshu devotees should also recognize kusang within satsang and should never associate with it. (224)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"225":{"sanskrit":["Harau gurau cha pratyakṣhe manuṣhya-bhāva-darshanaha;","Shithilo niyame yash-cha na tasya sangam ācharet. 225"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya pratyakṣh Bhagwānmā ane gurumā manuṣhyabhāv joto hoy ane niyam pāḷavāmā shithil hoy teno sang na karavo. (225)","english":"One should avoid the company of those who are lax in observing niyams or see human traits in the manifest form of Bhagwan or the guru. (225)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"226":{"sanskrit":["Bhakteṣhu doṣha-dṛuṣhṭih syād avaguṇaika-bhāṣhakaha;","Manasvī yo guru-drohī na cha tat-sangam ācharet. 226"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya bhaktomā doṣh jonār, avaguṇnī ja vāto karanār, manasvī ane gurudrohī hoy teno sang na karavo. (226)","english":"One should avoid the company of those who perceive drawbacks in devotees, speak only ill of others, are wilful or disobey the guru. (226)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"227":{"sanskrit":["Sat-kārya-nindako yash-cha sach-chhāstra-nindako janaha;","Satsanga-nindako yash-cha tat-sangam ācharen-na hi. 227"],"gujarati":"Je manuṣhya satkārya, sachchhāstra tathā satsangnī nindā karato hoy teno sang na karavo. (227)","english":"One should not associate with those who defame noble works, sacred texts or satsang. (227)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"228":{"sanskrit":["Vachanānām shruter yasya niṣhṭhāyā bhanjanam bhavet;","Gurau Harau cha satsange tasya sangam pari-tyajet. 228"],"gujarati":"Jenī vāto sāmbhaḷavāthī Bhagwān, guru tathā satsangne viṣhe niṣhṭhā ṭaḷatī hoy teno sang tyajavo. (228)","english":"One should shun the company of those whose words weaken one’s conviction in Bhagwan, the guru or satsang. (228)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"229":{"sanskrit":["Bhaved yo dṛuḍha-niṣhṭhāvān Akṣhara-Puruṣhottame;","Dṛuḍha-bhaktir-vivekī cha kuryāt tat-sangam ādarāt. 229"],"gujarati":"Jene Akṣhar-Puruṣhottamne viṣhe dṛuḍh niṣhṭhā hoy, dṛuḍh bhakti hoy ane je vivekī hoy teno sang ādar thakī karavo. (229)","english":"One should respectfully associate with a person who has firm devotion and conviction in Akshar-Purushottam and who is discerning. (229)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"230":{"sanskrit":["Harer-gurosh-cha vākyeṣhu shankā yasya na vidyate;","Vishvāsur buddhimān yash-cha kuryāt tat-sangam ādarāt. 230"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān tathā gurunā vākyomā jene sanshay na hoy, je vishvāsu hoy, buddhimān hoy teno sang ādar thakī karavo. (230)","english":"One should respectfully associate with those who do not doubt the words of Bhagwan or the guru, and are trustworthy and wise. (230)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"231":{"sanskrit":["Āgnāyāh pālane nityam sotsāham tat-paro dṛuḍhaha;","Nirmānah saralo yash-cha kuryāt tat-sangam ādarāt. 231"],"gujarati":"Āgnā pāḷavāmā je sadāy utsāh sāthe tatpar hoy, dṛuḍh hoy; je nirmānī tathā saraḷ hoy teno sang ādar thakī karavo. (231)","english":"One should respectfully associate with those who always eagerly follow commands with enthusiasm and determination, and are humble and cooperative. (231)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"232":{"sanskrit":["Harer gurosh-charitreṣhu divyeṣhu mānuṣheṣhu yah;","Sa-sneham divyatā-darshī kuryāt tat-sangam ādarāt. 232"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān ane gurunā divya tathā manuṣhya charitromā je sneh-pūrvak divyatānu darshan karato hoy teno sang ādar thakī karavo. (232)","english":"One should respectfully associate with those who lovingly see divinity in both the divine and human-like actions of Bhagwan and the guru. (232)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"233":{"sanskrit":["Tat-paro’nya-guṇa-grāhe vimukho dur-guṇoktitaha;","Suhṛud-bhāvī cha satsange kuryāt tat-sangam ādarāt. 233"],"gujarati":"Satsangmā je manuṣhya anyanā guṇo grahaṇ karavāmā tatpar hoy, durguṇonī vāt na karato hoy, suhṛudbhāvavāḷo hoy teno sang ādar thakī karavo. (233)","english":"One should respectfully associate with those in satsang who eagerly imbibe the virtues of others, never speak about others’ flaws and keep suhradbhāv. (233)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"234":{"sanskrit":["Lakṣhyam yasyaika-mātram syād Guruhari-prasannatā;","Āchāre’pi vichāre’pi kuryāt tat-sangam ādarāt. 234"],"gujarati":"Jenā āchār tathā vichārne viṣhe guruharine rājī karavānu ekamātra lakṣhya hoy teno sang ādar thakī karavo. (234)","english":"One should respectfully associate with a person whose conduct and thoughts aim solely to please the guru. (234)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"235":{"sanskrit":["Sva-sampradāya-granthānām yathā-shakti yathā-ruchi;","Sanskṛute prākṛute vā’pi kuryāt paṭhana-pāṭhane. 235"],"gujarati":"Potānī shakti ane ruchi pramāṇe Sanskṛut tathā prākṛut bhāṣhāmā potānā sampradāynā granthonu paṭhan-pāṭhan karavu. (235)","english":"One should study and teach the Sanskrit or vernacular texts of one’s Sampraday according to one’s abilities and preferences. (235)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"236":{"sanskrit":["Swāmi-vārtāhā paṭhen-nityam tathaiva Vachanāmṛutam;","Guṇātīta-gurūṇām cha charitam bhāvatah paṭhet. 236"],"gujarati":"Vachanāmṛut, Swāmīnī Vāto tathā guṇātīt guruonā jīvan-charitro nitye bhāvthī vānchavā. (236)","english":"One should daily read the Vachanamrut, Swamini Vato and the jivancharitras of the Gunatit gurus with adoration. (236)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"237":{"sanskrit":["Upadeshāsh-charitrāṇi Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho;","Guṇātīta-gurūṇām cha satsanginām hi jīvanam. 237"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān tathā guṇātīt guruonā updesho ane charitro satsangīonu jīvan chhe. Tethī satsangīe tenu shānt chitte shravaṇ, manan tathā nididhyāsan mahimāe sahit, shraddhā-pūrvak tathā bhaktithī roj karavu. (237-238)","english":"The teachings and actions of Swaminarayan Bhagwan and the Gunatit gurus are the very life of satsangis. Therefore, satsangis should, with a calm mind, listen to, contemplate on and repeatedly recall them daily with mahimā, faith and devotion. (237–238)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"238":{"sanskrit":["Atas-tach-chhravaṇam kuryād mananam nidi-dhyāsanam;","Mahimnā shraddhayā bhaktyā pratyaham shānta-chetasā. 238"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān tathā guṇātīt guruonā updesho ane charitro satsangīonu jīvan chhe. Tethī satsangīe tenu shānt chitte shravaṇ, manan tathā nididhyāsan mahimāe sahit, shraddhā-pūrvak tathā bhaktithī roj karavu. (237-238)","english":"The teachings and actions of Swaminarayan Bhagwan and the Gunatit gurus are the very life of satsangis. Therefore, satsangis should, with a calm mind, listen to, contemplate on and repeatedly recall them daily with mahimā, faith and devotion. (237–238)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"239":{"sanskrit":["Sāmpradāyika-siddhānta-bādhakaram hi yad vachaha;","Paṭhyam shravyam na mantavyam sanshayotpādakam cha yat. 239"],"gujarati":"Sampradāynā siddhāntomā bādh kare tathā sanshay utpanna kare tevā vachano vānchavā, sāmbhaḷavā ke mānavā nahī. (239)","english":"One should not read, listen to or believe words that go against the Sampraday’s principles or raise doubts. (239)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"240":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇe bhaktim parām dṛuḍhayitum hṛudi;","Guruhareh samādeshāch chāturmāsye vratam charet. 240"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānne viṣhe hṛudaymā parā-bhakti dṛuḍh karavā guruharinā ādeshthī Chāturmāsmā vrat karavu. (240)","english":"To reinforce profound devotion towards Swaminarayan Bhagwan in one’s heart, one should observe vows during Chāturmās according to the guru’s instructions. (240)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"241":{"sanskrit":["Chāndrāyaṇopavāsādir mantra-japah pradakṣhiṇāhā;","Kathā-shrutir-daṇḍavach-cha praṇāmā adhikās-tadā. 241"],"gujarati":"Temā chāndrāyaṇ, upavās vagere tathā mantra-jap, pradakṣhiṇā, kathā-shravaṇ, adhik danḍavat praṇām karavā ityādirūpe shraddhāe karīne, prīti-pūrvak ane Bhagwānno rājīpo prāpt karavā visheṣh bhaktinu ācharaṇ karavu. (241-242)","english":"This includes observing chāndrāyan and other fasts, as well as chanting the [Swaminarayan] mantra, performing pradakshinās, listening to spiritual discourses, offering extra dandvat pranāms, and additional devotion with faith, love and the wish to please Bhagwan. (241–242)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"242":{"sanskrit":["Ityevam ādirūpeṇa shraddhayā prīti-pūrvakam;","Hari-prasannatām prāptum visheṣhām bhaktim ācharet. 242"],"gujarati":"Temā chāndrāyaṇ, upavās vagere tathā mantra-jap, pradakṣhiṇā, kathā-shravaṇ, adhik danḍavat praṇām karavā ityādirūpe shraddhāe karīne, prīti-pūrvak ane Bhagwānno rājīpo prāpt karavā visheṣh bhaktinu ācharaṇ karavu. (241-242)","english":"This includes observing chāndrāyan and other fasts, as well as chanting the [Swaminarayan] mantra, performing pradakshinās, listening to spiritual discourses, offering extra dandvat pranāms, and additional devotion with faith, love and the wish to please Bhagwan. (241–242)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"243":{"sanskrit":["Sampradāyasya shāstrāṇām paṭhanam pāṭhanam tadā;","Yathā-ruchi yathā-shakti kuryād niyama-pūrvakam. 243"],"gujarati":"Tyāre potānī ruchi tathā shakti pramāṇe sampradāynā shāstronu niyam-pūrvak paṭhan-pāṭhan karavu. (243)","english":"During this time, one should also regularly read and teach the Sampraday’s shastras according to one’s preference and ability. (243)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"244":{"sanskrit":["Sarvaih satsangibhih kāryāh prītim vardhayitum Harau;","Utsavā bhakti-bhāvena harṣheṇollāsatas-tathā. 244"],"gujarati":"Bhagwānne viṣhe prīti vadhāravā sāru sarve satsangīoe harṣh ane ullāsthī bhaktibhāve utsavo karavā. (244)","english":"To increase one’s love for Bhagwan, all satsangis should celebrate festivals with great joy and devotion. (244)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"245":{"sanskrit":["Janma-mahotsavā nityam Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho;","Brahmā’kṣhara-gurūṇām cha kartavyā bhakti-bhāvataha. 245"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇ tathā Akṣharbrahma guruonā janma-mahotsavo bhakti-bhāvthī hammeshā ujavavā. (245)","english":"The birth festivals of Bhagwan Swaminarayan and the Aksharbrahman gurus should always be celebrated with devotion. (245)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"246":{"sanskrit":["Harer guror vishiṣhṭānām prasangānām dineṣhu cha;","Satsangibhir yathā-shakti kāryāh parvotsavā janaihi. 246"],"gujarati":"Satsangī janoe Shrīhari tathā gurunā vishiṣhṭa prasangone divase yathā-shakti parvotsavo karavā. (246)","english":"According to their means, satsangis should celebrate festivals to commemorate the special days related to Shri Hari and the gurus. (246)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"247":{"sanskrit":["Sa-vādyam kīrtanam kāryam parvotsaveṣhu bhaktitaha;","Mahimnash-cha kathā-vārtā karaṇīyā visheṣhataha. 247"],"gujarati":"Parvotsavone viṣhe bhaktie karīne savādya kīrtan karavu ane visheṣh karīne mahimānī vāto karavī. (247)","english":"During festivals, satsangis should devoutly sing kirtans to the accompaniment of instruments and especially discourse on the glory [of God and guru]. (247)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"248":{"sanskrit":["Chaitra-shukla-navamyām hi kāryam Shrī-Rāma-pūjanam;","Kṛuṣhṇā’ṣhṭamyām tu kartavyam Shrāvaṇe Kṛuṣhṇa-pūjanam. 248"],"gujarati":"Chaitra sud nomne divase Rāmchandra Bhagwānnu pūjan karavu. Shrāvaṇ vad āṭhamne divase Kṛuṣhṇa Bhagwānnu pūjan karavu. (248)","english":"On the day of Chaitra sud 9, one should offer pujan to Ramchandra Bhagwan. On the day of Shravan vad 8, one should offer pujan to Krishna Bhagwan. (248)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"249":{"sanskrit":["Shiva-rātrau hi kartavyam pūjanam Shankarasya cha;","Gaṇesham Bhādra-shuklāyām chaturthyām pūjayet tathā. 249"],"gujarati":"Shiva-rātrine viṣhe Shankar Bhagwānnu pūjan karavu. Bhādarvā sud chothne divase Gaṇpatinu pūjan karavu. (249)","english":"On Shivratri, one should offer pujan to Shankar Bhagwan. On Bhadarva sud 4, one should offer pujan to Ganpati. (249)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"250":{"sanskrit":["Mārutim Āshvine kṛuṣhṇa-chaturdashyām hi pūjayet;","Mārge mandira-samprāptau tad-devam praṇamed hṛudā. 250"],"gujarati":"Āso vad chaudashne divas Hanumānjīnu pūjan karavu. Mārge jatā koī mandir āve to te devne bhāvthī praṇām karavā. (250)","english":"On Aso vad 14, one should offer pujan to Hanumanji. One should devoutly bow to the deities of any mandir that one comes across. (250)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"251":{"sanskrit":["Viṣhṇush-cha Shankarash-chaiva Pārvatī cha Gajānanaha;","Dina-karash-cha panchaitā mānyāh pūjyā hi devatāhā. 251"],"gujarati":"Viṣhṇu, Shankar, Pārvatī, Gaṇpati tathā Sūrya e pānch devatā pūjyapaṇe mānavā. (251)","english":"Vishnu, Shankar, Parvati, Ganpati and Surya – these five deities should be revered. (251)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"252":{"sanskrit":["Pari-rakṣhed dṛuḍhām niṣhṭhām Akṣhara-Puruṣhottame;","Tathā’pi naiva kartavyam devatā’ntara-nindanam. 252"],"gujarati":"Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne viṣhe dṛuḍh niṣhṭhā rākhavī. Tem chhatā koī paṇ anya devonī nindā na karavī. (252)","english":"One should have firm conviction in Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj. However, one should not disrespect any other deity. (252)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"253":{"sanskrit":["Dharmā vā sampradāyā vā ye’nye tad-anuyāyinaha;","Na te dveṣhyā na te nindyā ādartavyāsh-cha sarvadā. 253"],"gujarati":"Anya dharmo, sampradāyo ke temanā anuyāyīone viṣhe dveṣh na karavo. Temanī nindā na karavī. Temane sadā ādar āpavo. (253)","english":"One should not have contempt for other religions, sampradāys or their followers. One should never criticize them and should always treat them with respect. (253)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"254":{"sanskrit":["Mandirāṇi cha shāstrāṇi santas-tathā kadāchana;","Na nindyāste hi satkāryā yathā-shakti yathochitam. 254"],"gujarati":"Mandiro, shāstro ane santonī kyārey nindā na karavī. Potānī shakti pramāṇe temano yathochit satkār karavo. (254)","english":"One should never disrespect mandirs, shastras or sadhus. One should honour them appropriately according to one’s capacity. (254)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"255":{"sanskrit":["Sanyam-anopavāsādi yad-yat-tapah samācharet;","Prasādāya Hares-tat tu bhaktyartham eva kevalam. 255"],"gujarati":"Sanyam, upavās ityādi je je tapnu ācharaṇ karavu te to kevaḷ Bhagwānne rājī karavā tathā bhakti māṭe ja karavu. (255)","english":"Whichever acts of self-control, fasts and other austerities are undertaken, they should be performed only as bhakti and with the intent to solely please Bhagwan. (255)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"256":{"sanskrit":["Ekādashyā vratam nityam kartavyam param-ādarāt;","Tad-dine naiva bhoktavyam niṣhiddham vastu karhichit. 256"],"gujarati":"Ekādashīnu vrat sadāy param ādar thakī karavu. Te divase niṣhiddha vastu kyārey na jamavī. (256)","english":"One should always observe the ekādashi fast with utmost reverence. On this day, prohibited items should never be consumed. (256)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"257":{"sanskrit":["Upavāse divā-nidrām prayatnatah pari-tyajet;","Divasa-nidrayā nashyed upavāsātmakam tapaha. 257"],"gujarati":"Upavāsne viṣhe divasnī nidrāno prayatna-pūrvak tyāg karavo. Divase līdhelī nidrāthī upavāsrūpī tap nāsh pāme chhe. (257)","english":"While fasting, one should endeavor to give up sleep during daytime. Sleeping during daytime destroys the merits earned by the austerity of fasting. (257)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"258":{"sanskrit":["Swāminārāyaṇeneha swayam yaddhi prasāditam;","Gurubhish-chā’kṣhara-Brahma-swarūpair yat prasāditam. 258"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇe pote je sthānone prasādībhūt karyā chhe, Akṣharbrahma-swarūp guruoe je sthānone prasādībhūt karyā chhe, te sthānonī yātrā karavānī ichchhā hoy teṇe potānī shakti ane ruchi pramāṇe karavī. (258-259)","english":"If one desires to go on a pilgrimage to the places sanctified by Bhagwan Swaminarayan or the Aksharbrahman gurus, one should do so according to one’s means and preferences. (258–259)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"259":{"sanskrit":["Teṣhām sthāna-visheṣhāṇām yātrām kartum ya ichchhati;","Tad yātrām sa janah kuryād yathā-shakti yathā-ruchi. 259"],"gujarati":"Bhagwān Swāminārāyaṇe pote je sthānone prasādībhūt karyā chhe, Akṣharbrahma-swarūp guruoe je sthānone prasādībhūt karyā chhe, te sthānonī yātrā karavānī ichchhā hoy teṇe potānī shakti ane ruchi pramāṇe karavī. (258-259)","english":"If one desires to go on a pilgrimage to the places sanctified by Bhagwan Swaminarayan or the Aksharbrahman gurus, one should do so according to one’s means and preferences. (258–259)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"260":{"sanskrit":["Ayodhyām Mathurām Kāshīm Kedāram Badarīm vrajet;","Rāmeshvarādi tīrtham cha yathā-shakti yathā-ruchi. 260"],"gujarati":"Ayodhyā, Mathurā, Kāshī, Kedārnāth, Badrīnāth tathā Rāmeshvar ityādi tīrthonī yātrāe potānī shakti ane ruchi pramāṇe javu. (260)","english":"One may go on a pilgrimage to Ayodhya, Mathura, Kashi, Kedarnath, Badrinath, Rameshwar and other sacred places according to one’s means and preferences. (260)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"261":{"sanskrit":["Maryādā pālanīyaiva sarvair mandiram āgataihi;","Nāryo naiva naraih spṛushyā nārībhish-cha narās-tathā. 261"],"gujarati":"Mandirmā āvel sau koīe maryādānu pālan avashya karavu. Mandirne viṣhe āvel puruṣhoe strīno sparsh na karavo tathā strīoe puruṣhno sparsh na karavo. (261)","english":"After arriving at the mandir, all should certainly follow its disciplines. Males should not touch females and females should not touch males. (261)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"262":{"sanskrit":["Niyamam anusṛutyaiva satsangasya tu mandire;","Vastrāṇi pari-dheyāni strībhih pumbhish-cha sarvadā. 262"],"gujarati":"Strīo tathā puruṣhoe hammeshā satsangnā niyam anusār mandirne viṣhe vastro paheravā. (262)","english":"At the mandir, males and females should always dress according to the norms of satsang. (262)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"263":{"sanskrit":["Gachchhed yadā darshanārtham bhakta-jano Harer guroho;","Riktena pāṇinā naiva gachchhet tadā kadāchana. 263"],"gujarati":"Bhaktajane Bhagwān ke gurunā darshane kyārey khālī hāthe na javu. (263)","english":"A devotee should never go empty-handed for the darshan of Bhagwan or the guru. (263)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"264":{"sanskrit":["Āditya-chandrayor grāha-kāle satsangibhih samaihi;","Pari-tyajya kriyāhā sarvāh kartavyam bhajanam Harehe. 264"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangīoe sūrya ke chandranā grahaṇ kāḷe sarva kriyāono tyāg karī Bhagwānnu bhajan karavu. Te samaye nidrā tathā bhojanno tyāg karīne ek sthaḷe besīne grahaṇ pūrṇa thāy tyā sudhī bhagwat-kīrtanādi karavu. (264-265)","english":"During a solar or lunar eclipse, all satsangis should discontinue all activities and engage in Bhagwan’s bhajan. During that time, one should not sleep or eat, but sit in one place to sing kirtans dedicated to Bhagwan and undertake other forms of devotion until the eclipse is over. (264– 265)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"265":{"sanskrit":["Nidrām cha bhojanam tyaktvā tadaikatropavishya cha;","Kartavyam grāha-muktyantam Bhagavat-kīrtanādikam. 265"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangīoe sūrya ke chandranā grahaṇ kāḷe sarva kriyāono tyāg karī Bhagwānnu bhajan karavu. Te samaye nidrā tathā bhojanno tyāg karīne ek sthaḷe besīne grahaṇ pūrṇa thāy tyā sudhī bhagwat-kīrtanādi karavu. (264-265)","english":"During a solar or lunar eclipse, all satsangis should discontinue all activities and engage in Bhagwan’s bhajan. During that time, one should not sleep or eat, but sit in one place to sing kirtans dedicated to Bhagwan and undertake other forms of devotion until the eclipse is over. (264– 265)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"266":{"sanskrit":["Grāha-muktau sa-vastram hi kāryam snānam samair janaihi;","Tyāgibhish-cha Harihi pūjyo deyam dānam gṛuhasthitaihi. 266"],"gujarati":"Grahaṇnī mukti thaye sarva janoe savastra snān karavu. Tyāgīoe Bhagwānnī pūjā karavī ane gṛuhasthoe dān karavu. (266)","english":"When the eclipse is over, all should bathe and soak the clothes they are wearing. Thereafter, renunciants should perform puja and householder devotees should give donations. (266)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"267":{"sanskrit":["Janmano maraṇasyā’pi vidhayah sūtakādayaha;","Satsanga-rītim-āshritya pālyāh shrāddhā-dayas-tathā. 267"],"gujarati":"Janma-maraṇnī sūtak tathā shrāddha vagere vidhio satsangnī rītne anusarī pāḷavī. (267)","english":"One should perform rituals related to birth, death and shrāddh according to the Satsang tradition. (267)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"268":{"sanskrit":["Prāyash-chittam anuṣhṭheyam jāte tvayogya-vartane;","Paramātma-prasādārtham shuddhena bhāvatas-tadā. 268"],"gujarati":"Koī ayogya ācharaṇ thaī jāy tyāre Bhagwānne rājī karavā shuddha bhāve prāyashchitta karavu. (268)","english":"If one has acted immorally, one should piously atone to please Bhagwan. (268)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"269":{"sanskrit":["Āpat-kāle tu satyeva hyāpado dharmam ācharet;","Alpāpattim mahāpattim matvā dharmam na san-tyajet. 269"],"gujarati":"Āpatkāḷmā ja āpaddharma ācharavo. Alp āpattine moṭī āpatti mānī laī dharmano tyāg na karavo. (269)","english":"One should follow the rules described for emergencies only in times of crisis. Do not give up one’s dharma by considering minor difficulties to be major. (269)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"270":{"sanskrit":["Āpattau kaṣhṭa-dāyām tu rakṣhā svasya parasya cha;","Yathaiva syāt tathā kāryam rakṣhatā Bhagavad-balam. 270"],"gujarati":"Kaṣhṭ āpe tevī āpatti āvī paḍe tyāre Bhagwānnu baḷ rākhī je rīte potānī tathā anyanī rakṣhā thāy tem karavu. (270)","english":"When agonizing calamities arise, one should derive strength from Bhagwan and act to protect oneself and others. (270)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"271":{"sanskrit":["Āpattau prāṇa-nāshinyām prāptāyām tu vivekinā;","Gurvādeshā’nusāreṇa prāṇān rakṣhet sukham vaset. 271"],"gujarati":"Vivekī manuṣhye prāṇno nāsh thāy tevī āpatti āvī paḍe tyāre gurunā ādeshone anusarīne prāṇnī rakṣhā karavī ane sukhe rahevu. (271)","english":"When faced with circumstances that may result in death, one who is wise should act according to the guru’s teachings to protect one’s life and live peacefully. (271)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"272":{"sanskrit":["Satsanga-rītim-āshritya gurvādeshā’nusārataha;","Pari-shuddhena bhāvena sarvaih satsangibhir janaihi. 272"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangī janoe satsangnī rīt pramāṇe, gurunā ādesh anusār, parishuddha bhāvthī desh, kāḷ, avasthā tathā potānī shakti pramāṇe āchār, vyavahār ane prāyashchit karavā. (272-273)","english":"As per their prevailing location, time, age and abilities, all satsangis should genuinely act, atone and engage in dealings according to the traditions of the Satsang and the guru’s instructions. (272–273)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"273":{"sanskrit":["Desham kālam avasthām cha sva-shaktim anusṛutya cha;","Āchāro vyavahārash-cha prāyash-chittam vidhīyatām. 273"],"gujarati":"Sarve satsangī janoe satsangnī rīt pramāṇe, gurunā ādesh anusār, parishuddha bhāvthī desh, kāḷ, avasthā tathā potānī shakti pramāṇe āchār, vyavahār ane prāyashchit karavā. (272-273)","english":"As per their prevailing location, time, age and abilities, all satsangis should genuinely act, atone and engage in dealings according to the traditions of the Satsang and the guru’s instructions. (272–273)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"274":{"sanskrit":["Jīvanam unnatim yāti dharma-niyama-pālanāt;","Anyashchā’pi sadāchāra-pālane prerito bhavet. 274"],"gujarati":"Dharma-niyam pāḷavāthī jīvan unnat thāy chhe ane anyane paṇ sadāchār pāḷavānī preraṇā maḷe chhe. (274)","english":"Observing dharma and niyams elevates the quality of one’s life and also inspires others to live righteously. (274)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"275":{"sanskrit":["Bhūta-preta-pishāchāder bhayam kadāpi nā’pnuyāt;","Īdṛuk shankāh pari-tyajya haribhaktah sukham vaset. 275"],"gujarati":"Bhagwānnā bhakte kyārey bhūt, pret, pishāch ādinī bīk na rākhavī. Āvī āshankāono tyāg karīne sukhe rahevu. (275)","english":"Devotees of Bhagwan should never fear evil spirits, such as bhuts, prets or pishāchas. They should give up such apprehensions and live happily. (275)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"276":{"sanskrit":["Shubhā’shubha-prasangeṣhu mahima-sahitam janaha;","Pavitrām Sahajānanda-Nāmāvalim paṭhet tathā. 276"],"gujarati":"Shubh tathā ashubh prasangone viṣhe mahimāe sahit pavitra Sahajānand Nāmāvalīno pāṭh karavo. (276)","english":"On auspicious and inauspicious occasions, one should recite the sacred ‘Sahajanand Namavali’ while understanding its glory. (276)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"277":{"sanskrit":["Kālo vā karma vā māyā prabhaven-naiva karhichit;","Aniṣhṭa-karaṇe nūnam satsangā’shraya-shālinām. 277"],"gujarati":"Jeone satsangno āshray thayo chhe temanu kāḷ, karma ke māyā kyārey aniṣhṭ karavā samarth thatā ja nathī. (277)","english":"Kāl, karma and māyā can never harm those who have taken refuge in satsang. (277)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"278":{"sanskrit":["Ayogya-viṣhayāsh-chaivam ayogya-vyasanāni cha;","Āshankāh sampari-tyājyāh satsangam āshritaih sadā. 278"],"gujarati":"Satsangīoe ayogya viṣhayo, vyasano tathā vahemno sadāy tyāg karavo. (278)","english":"Satsangis should always renounce inappropriate indulgence in the sense pleasures, addictions and superstitions. (278)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"279":{"sanskrit":["Naiva manyeta kartṛutvam kāla-karmādikasya tu;","Manyeta sarva-kartāram Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam. 279"],"gujarati":"Kāḷ, karma ādinu kartāpaṇu na mānavu. Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne sarva-kartā mānavā. (279)","english":"Do not believe kāl, karma and other factors to be the doers. One should realize Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj as the all-doer. (279)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"280":{"sanskrit":["Vipattiṣhu dhared dhairyam prārthanam yatnam ācharet;","Bhajeta dṛuḍha-vishvāsam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottame. 280"],"gujarati":"Vipatti āve tyāre dhīraj rākhavī, prārthanā karavī, prayatna karavo ane Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne viṣhe dṛuḍh vishvās rākhavo. (280)","english":"In difficult times, one should remain patient, offer prayers, persevere and keep firm faith in Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj. (280)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"281":{"sanskrit":["Tyāgā’shramechchhunā dīkṣhā grāhyā Brahmā’kṣharād guroho;","Brahma-charyam sadā sarvaih pālyam tyāgibhir aṣhṭadhā. 281"],"gujarati":"Tyāgāshram grahaṇ karavānī ichchhā hoy temaṇe Akṣharbrahma-swarūp guru pāse dīkṣhā grahaṇ karavī. Sarve tyāgīoe sadā aṣhṭa-prakāre brahmacharya pāḷavu. (281)","english":"Those who wish to join the sadhu āshram should receive initiation from the Aksharbrahman guru. All sadhus should always observe eight-fold brahmacharya. (281)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"282":{"sanskrit":["Dhanam tu tyāgibhis-tyājyam rakṣhyam svīyatayā na cha;","Spṛushyam naivā’pi vittam cha tyāgibhis-tu kadāchana. 282"],"gujarati":"Tyāgīoe dhanno tyāg karavo ane potānu karīne rākhavu nahī. Dhanno sparsh paṇ na ja karavo. (282)","english":"Renunciants should renounce money and should not keep it as their own. They should not even touch money. (282)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"283":{"sanskrit":["Tyāgibhih prīti-vṛuddhyartham Akṣhara-Puruṣhottame;","Niṣhkāmatvam sadā dhāryam nirlobhatvam sadaiva cha. 283"],"gujarati":"Tyāgīoe Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne viṣhe prīti vadhāravā sāru sadā niṣhkāmpaṇu, nirlobhpaṇu, nihswādpaṇu, nihsnehpaṇu, nirmānpaṇu tathā tyāgīnā anya guṇo dhāraṇ karavā. (283-284)","english":"To increase their love for Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj, renunciants should always imbibe the virtues of nishkām, nirlobh, nissvād, nissneh, nirmān, and the other ascetic qualities. (283–284)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"284":{"sanskrit":["Nihsvādatvam sadā dhāryam nihsnehatvam tathaiva cha;","Nirmānatvam sadā dhāryam anye cha tyāgino guṇāhā. 284"],"gujarati":"Tyāgīoe Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne viṣhe prīti vadhāravā sāru sadā niṣhkāmpaṇu, nirlobhpaṇu, nihswādpaṇu, nihsnehpaṇu, nirmānpaṇu tathā tyāgīnā anya guṇo dhāraṇ karavā. (283-284)","english":"To increase their love for Akshar- Purushottam Maharaj, renunciants should always imbibe the virtues of nishkām, nirlobh, nissvād, nissneh, nirmān, and the other ascetic qualities. (283–284)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"285":{"sanskrit":["Svā’tma-brahmaikatām prāpya Swāminārāyaṇo Harihi;","Sarvadā bhajanīyo hi tyāgibhir divyabhāvataha. 285"],"gujarati":"Tyāgīoe potānā ātmānī brahma sangāthe ekatā prāpt karīne divyabhāve sadāy Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānne bhajavā. (285)","english":"Renunciants should identify their ātmā with Brahman and always offer devotion to Swaminarayan Bhagwan with divyabhāv. (285)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"286":{"sanskrit":["Tyāgo na kevalam tyāgas-tyāgo bhakti-mayas-tvayam;","Pari-tyāgo hyayam prāptum Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamam. 286"],"gujarati":"Tyāg e kevaḷ tyāg ja nathī parantu ā tyāg to bhaktimay chhe. Ā tyāg Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārājne pāmavā māṭe chhe. (286)","english":"Renunciation is not merely self-denial; it is also endowed with devotion. Such renunciation is for attaining Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj. (286)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"287":{"sanskrit":["Āgnopāsana-siddhāntāh sarva-jīva-hitāvahāhā;","Dukha-vināshakā ete parama-sukha-dāyakāhā. 287"],"gujarati":"Āgnā-upāsanā sambandhī ā siddhānto sarva-jīva-hitāvah chhe, dukh-vināshak chhe ane param-sukh-dāyak chhe. (287)","english":"These principles of āgnā and upāsanā are beneficial to all; they destroy misery and bestow utmost bliss. (287)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"288":{"sanskrit":["Etachchhāstrānusāreṇa yah prītyā shraddhayā janaha;","Āgnopāsanayor dārḍhyam prakuryāt svasya jīvane. 288"],"gujarati":"Ā shāstrane anusarīne je jan shraddhā ane prītithī potānā jīvanmā āgnā-upāsanānī dṛuḍhatā kare, te Bhagwānno rājīpo prāpt karī temanī kṛupānu pātra thāy chhe. Shāstromā kahel brāhmī sthitine te jīvatā chhatā ja prāpt kare chhe. Ekāntik dharma siddha kare chhe. Bhagwānnā shāshvat, divya evā Akṣhardhāmne pāme chhe, ātyantik mukti meḷave chhe ane sukh prāpt kare chhe. (288-290)","english":"Those who faithfully and lovingly strengthen āgnā and upāsanā in their life according to this shastra earn the pleasure of Bhagwan and become a recipient of his grace. While living, they attain the brāhmi sthiti described in the shastras. They master ekāntik dharma. They attain the eternal and divine Akshardham of Bhagwan, ultimate moksha and bliss. (288–290)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"289":{"sanskrit":["Harehe prasannatām prāpya tat-kṛupā-bhājano bhavet;","Jīvan-neva sthitim brāhmīn shāstroktām āpnuyāt sa cha. 289"],"gujarati":"Ā shāstrane anusarīne je jan shraddhā ane prītithī potānā jīvanmā āgnā-upāsanānī dṛuḍhatā kare, te Bhagwānno rājīpo prāpt karī temanī kṛupānu pātra thāy chhe. Shāstromā kahel brāhmī sthitine te jīvatā chhatā ja prāpt kare chhe. Ekāntik dharma siddha kare chhe. Bhagwānnā shāshvat, divya evā Akṣhardhāmne pāme chhe, ātyantik mukti meḷave chhe ane sukh prāpt kare chhe. (288-290)","english":"Those who faithfully and lovingly strengthen āgnā and upāsanā in their life according to this shastra earn the pleasure of Bhagwan and become a recipient of his grace. While living, they attain the brāhmi sthiti described in the shastras. They master ekāntik dharma. They attain the eternal and divine Akshardham of Bhagwan, ultimate moksha and bliss. (288–290)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"290":{"sanskrit":["Dharmaikāntika-sansiddhim āpnute divyam Akṣharam;","Shāshvatam Bhagavad-dhāma muktim-ātyantikīm sukham. 290"],"gujarati":"Ā shāstrane anusarīne je jan shraddhā ane prītithī potānā jīvanmā āgnā-upāsanānī dṛuḍhatā kare, te Bhagwānno rājīpo prāpt karī temanī kṛupānu pātra thāy chhe. Shāstromā kahel brāhmī sthitine te jīvatā chhatā ja prāpt kare chhe. Ekāntik dharma siddha kare chhe. Bhagwānnā shāshvat, divya evā Akṣhardhāmne pāme chhe, ātyantik mukti meḷave chhe ane sukh prāpt kare chhe. (288-290)","english":"Those who faithfully and lovingly strengthen āgnā and upāsanā in their life according to this shastra earn the pleasure of Bhagwan and become a recipient of his grace. While living, they attain the brāhmi sthiti described in the shastras. They master ekāntik dharma. They attain the eternal and divine Akshardham of Bhagwan, ultimate moksha and bliss. (288–290)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"291":{"sanskrit":["Akṣharabrahma-sādharmyam samprāpya dāsa-bhāvataha;","Puruṣhottama-bhaktir hi muktir ātyantikī matā. 291"],"gujarati":"Akṣharbrahmanu sādharmya prāpt karī Puruṣhottamnī dāsbhāve bhakti karavī e mukti mānavāmā āvī chhe. (291)","english":"Attaining oneness with Aksharbrahman and offering humble devotion to Purushottam is considered to be mukti. (291)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"292":{"sanskrit":["Sankṣhipyā’tra kṛutam hyevam āgnopāsana-varṇanam;","Tad vistaram vijānīyāt sāmpradāyika-shāstrataha. 292"],"gujarati":"Ā rīte sankṣhepe karīne ahī āgnā tathā upāsanānu varṇan karyu. Teno vistār sampradāynā shāstro thakī jāṇavo. (292)","english":"Here, in this way, āgnā and upāsanā have been concisely described. One should obtain further details from the Sampraday’s shastras. (292)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"293":{"sanskrit":["Etat-Satsanga-Dīkṣheti shāstrasya prati-vāsaram;","Kāryah satsangibhih pāṭha ekāgra-chetasā janaihi. 293"],"gujarati":"Satsangī janoe pratidin ā ‘Satsang-Dīkṣhā’ shāstrano ekāgra chitte pāṭh karavo. Pāṭh karavā asamarth hoy temaṇe prīti-pūrvak tenu shravaṇ karavu. Ane shraddhāthī te rīte ācharavā prayatna karavo. (293-294)","english":"Satsangis should daily read this ‘Satsang Diksha’ shastra with concentration. Those who are unable to read should lovingly listen to it. Moreover, all should faithfully endeavor to practice it. (293–294)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"294":{"sanskrit":["Paṭhane chā’samarthais-tu shravyam tat prīti-pūrvakam;","Ācharitum cha kartavyah prayatnah shraddhayā tathā. 294"],"gujarati":"Satsangī janoe pratidin ā ‘Satsang-Dīkṣhā’ shāstrano ekāgra chitte pāṭh karavo. Pāṭh karavā asamarth hoy temaṇe prīti-pūrvak tenu shravaṇ karavu. Ane shraddhāthī te rīte ācharavā prayatna karavo. (293-294)","english":"Satsangis should daily read this ‘Satsang Diksha’ shastra with concentration. Those who are unable to read should lovingly listen to it. Moreover, all should faithfully endeavor to practice it. (293–294)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"295":{"sanskrit":["Paramātmā Param Brahma Swāminārāyaṇo Harihi;","Siddhāntam sthāpayāmāsa hyakṣhara-Puruṣhottamam. 295"],"gujarati":"Paramātmā Parabrahma Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwāne Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam siddhāntnī sthāpanā karī ane guṇātīt guruoe tenu pravartan karyu. Te siddhānt anusār ā shāstra rachyu chhe. (295-296)","english":"The Akshar-Purushottam siddhānt was established by Paramatma Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan and spread by the Gunatit gurus. This shastra is written based on this siddhānt. (295–296)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"296":{"sanskrit":["Guravash-cha Guṇātītāsh-cha-krustasya pravartanam;","Virachitam idam shāstram tat-siddhāntā’nusārataha. 296"],"gujarati":"Paramātmā Parabrahma Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwāne Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam siddhāntnī sthāpanā karī ane guṇātīt guruoe tenu pravartan karyu. Te siddhānt anusār ā shāstra rachyu chhe. (295-296)","english":"The Akshar-Purushottam siddhānt was established by Paramatma Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan and spread by the Gunatit gurus. This shastra is written based on this siddhānt. (295–296)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"297":{"sanskrit":["Kṛupayaivā’vatīrṇo’tra mumukṣhu-mokṣha-hetunā;","Parabrahma dayālur hi Swāminārāyaṇo bhuvi. 297"],"gujarati":"Parabrahma dayāḷu Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān kṛupāe karīne ja mumukṣhuonā mokṣha māṭe ā lokmā avataryā. Sakaḷ āshrit bhaktonā yog-kṣhemnu vahan karyu ane ā lok tathā paralok em banne prakārnu emaṇe kalyāṇ karyu. (297-298)","english":"To grant moksha to the mumukshus, the compassionate Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan manifested on this earth out of sheer grace. For all devotees who sought refuge he provided for their well-being and prosperity. He benefited them both in this world and beyond. (297–298)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"298":{"sanskrit":["Sakalā’shrita-bhaktānām yoga-kṣhemau tathā’vahat;","Vyadhāt sa dvi-vidham shreya āmuṣhmikam tathaihikam. 298"],"gujarati":"Parabrahma dayāḷu Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān kṛupāe karīne ja mumukṣhuonā mokṣha māṭe ā lokmā avataryā. Sakaḷ āshrit bhaktonā yog-kṣhemnu vahan karyu ane ā lok tathā paralok em banne prakārnu emaṇe kalyāṇ karyu. (297-298)","english":"To grant moksha to the mumukshus, the compassionate Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan manifested on this earth out of sheer grace. For all devotees who sought refuge he provided for their well-being and prosperity. He benefited them both in this world and beyond. (297–298)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"299":{"sanskrit":["Sarvatraivā’bhivarṣhantu sadā divyāh kṛupā’shiṣhaha;","Paramātma-Parabrahma-Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho. 299"],"gujarati":"Sarvatra Paramātmā Parabrahma Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnā divya kṛupāshiṣh sadā varase. (299)","english":"May the divine, compassionate blessings of Paramatma Parabrahman Swaminarayan Bhagwan always shower everywhere. (299)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"300":{"sanskrit":["Sarveṣhām sarva-dukhāni tāpa-trayam upadravāhā;","Kleshās-tathā vinashyeyur agnānam sanshayā bhayam. 300"],"gujarati":"Sarvenā sarva dukho, traṇ tāp, upadravo, klesho, agnān, sanshayo tathā bhay vināsh pāme. (300)","english":"May all grief, the three types of miseries, calamities, distresses, ignorance, doubts and fears of all be destroyed. (300)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"301":{"sanskrit":["Bhagavat-kṛupayā sarve svāsthyam nirāmayam sukham;","Prāpnuvantu parām shāntim kalyāṇam paramam tathā. 301"],"gujarati":"Bhagwānnī kṛupāthī sarve nirāmay swāsthya, sukh, param shānti tathā param kalyāṇ pāmo. (301)","english":"Through Bhagwan’s grace, may all attain good health, happiness, utmost peace and ultimate moksha. (301)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"302":{"sanskrit":["Na kashchit kasyachit kuryād droham dveṣham tathā janaha;","Sevantām ādaram sarve sarvadaiva parasparam. 302"],"gujarati":"Koī manuṣhya koīno droh tathā dveṣh na kare. Sarve sadāy paraspar ādar seve. (302)","english":"May no one harm or hate others. May everyone always respect each other. (302)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"303":{"sanskrit":["Sarveṣhām jāyatām prītir dṛuḍhā niṣhṭhā cha nishchayaha;","Vishvāso vardhatām nityam Akṣhara-Puruṣhottame. 303"],"gujarati":"Akṣhar-Puruṣhottamne viṣhe sarvane dṛuḍh prīti, niṣhṭhā, nishchay thāy ane vishvās sadāy vṛuddhi pāme. (303)","english":"May everyone develop firm love, conviction and unwavering belief in Akshar-Purushottam, and may everyone’s faith forever flourish. (303)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"304":{"sanskrit":["Bhavantu balinah sarve bhaktāsh-cha dharma-pālane;","Āpnuyuh Sahajānanda-Parātmanah prasannatām. 304"],"gujarati":"Sarve bhakto dharma pāḷavāmā baḷiyā thāy ane Sahajānand Paramātmānī prasannatā prāpt kare. (304)","english":"May all devotees become resolute in following dharma and attain the pleasure of Sahajanand Paramatma. (304)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"305":{"sanskrit":["Prashāntair jāyatām yukto manuṣhyair dharma-shālibhihi;","Sansārah sādhanā-shīlair adhyātma-mārga-sansthitaihi. 305"],"gujarati":"Sansār prashānt, dharmavān, sādhanāshīl tathā adhyātma-mārge chālanārā manuṣhyothī yukta thāy. (305)","english":"May the world be filled with people who are peaceful, righteous and engrossed in spiritual endeavours, and who tread the path of spirituality. (305)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"306":{"sanskrit":["Aikyam mithah suhṛud-bhāvo maitrī kāruṇyam eva cha;","Sahana-shīlatā snehah sarva-janeṣhu vardhatām. 306"],"gujarati":"Sarva manuṣhyomā paraspar ekatā, suhṛudbhāv, maitrī, karuṇā, sahan-shīlatā tathā sneh vṛuddhi pāme. (306)","english":"May mutual unity, suhradbhāv, friendship, compassion, tolerance and love flourish among all people. (306)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"307":{"sanskrit":["Satsange divya-sambandhād Brahmaṇah Parabrahmaṇaha;","Sarveṣhām jāyatām dārḍhyam nirdoṣha-divya-bhāvayoho. 307"],"gujarati":"Brahma tathā Parabrahmanā divya sambandhe karīne satsangne viṣhe sarvane nirdoṣhbhāv tathā divyabhāvnī dṛuḍhatā thāy. (307)","english":"Through the divine association of Brahman and Parabrahman, may all strengthen nirdoshbhāv and divyabhāv towards the Satsang. (307)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"308":{"sanskrit":["Akṣhara-rūpatām sarve samprāpya svātmani janāhā;","Prāpnuyuh Sahajānande bhaktim hi Puruṣhottame. 308"],"gujarati":"Sarva jano potānā ātmāne viṣhe akṣharrūptā prāpt karī Puruṣhottam Sahajānandnī bhakti prāpt kare. (308)","english":"May all identify their ātmā as aksharrup and offer devotion to Purushottam Sahajanand. (308)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"309":{"sanskrit":["Māghasya shukla-panchamyām ārabdham asya lekhanam;","Pavitre vikramābde hi rasarṣhi-kha-dvi-sanmite. 309"],"gujarati":"Vikram samvat 2076nā Māgh shukla panchamīe ā shāstra lakhavāno ārambh karyo ane Chaitra sud navamīe Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnā divya janma-mahotsave te sampūrṇ thayu. (309-310)","english":"The writing of this shastra began on Magha (Maha) sud 5 [30 January 2020 CE] of Vikram Samvat 2076 and was completed on Chaitra sud 9 [2 April 2020 CE], on the divine birthday celebration of Swaminarayan Bhagwan. (309–310)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"310":{"sanskrit":["Chaitra-shukla-navamyām cha Swāminārāyaṇa-Prabhoho;","Tach-cha sampūrṇatām prāptam divya-janma-mahotsave. 310"],"gujarati":"Vikram samvat 2076nā Māgh shukla panchamīe ā shāstra lakhavāno ārambh karyo ane Chaitra sud navamīe Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwānnā divya janma-mahotsave te sampūrṇ thayu. (309-310)","english":"The writing of this shastra began on Magha (Maha) sud 5 [30 January 2020 CE] of Vikram Samvat 2076 and was completed on Chaitra sud 9 [2 April 2020 CE], on the divine birthday celebration of Swaminarayan Bhagwan. (309–310)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"311":{"sanskrit":["Upāsya-Sahajānanda-Haraye Parabrahmaṇe;","Mūlā’kṣhara-Guṇātītānandāya Swāmine tathā. 311"],"gujarati":"Upāsya Parabrahma Sahajānand Shrīhari tathā Mūḷ Akṣhar Guṇātītānand Swāmī, sākṣhād gnān-mūrti samā Bhagatjī Mahārāj, satya siddhāntnā rakṣhak evā Yagnapuruṣhdāsjī (Shāstrījī Mahārāj), sadāy vātsalya-bhīnā ane ānandmay brahma evā Yogījī Mahārāj tathā vishva-vandya ane vinamra evā guru Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājne ā shāstrarūpī anjali Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājnā janma shatābdī parve sānand bhakti-bhāve arpaṇ karavāmā āve chhe. (311-314)","english":"On the occasion of Pramukh Swami Maharaj’s birth centenary celebrations, this shastra is being offered with joy and devotion as a tribute to: (1) Parabrahman Sahajanand Shri Hari – the focus of upāsanā, (2) Mul Akshar Gunatitanand Swami, (3) Bhagatji Maharaj – the embodiment of wisdom, (4) Yagnapurushdasji (Shastriji Maharaj) – the protector of the true siddhānt, (5) the forever affectionate and blissful embodiment of Aksharbrahman, Yogiji Maharaj and (6) Guru Pramukh Swami Maharaj, who is humble and revered throughout the world. (311–314)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"312":{"sanskrit":["Bhagatajī-Mahārāja-sākṣhād-vignāna-mūrtaye;","Yagnapuruṣhadāsāya satya-siddhānta-rakṣhiṇe. 312"],"gujarati":"Upāsya Parabrahma Sahajānand Shrīhari tathā Mūḷ Akṣhar Guṇātītānand Swāmī, sākṣhād gnān-mūrti samā Bhagatjī Mahārāj, satya siddhāntnā rakṣhak evā Yagnapuruṣhdāsjī (Shāstrījī Mahārāj), sadāy vātsalya-bhīnā ane ānandmay brahma evā Yogījī Mahārāj tathā vishva-vandya ane vinamra evā guru Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājne ā shāstrarūpī anjali Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājnā janma shatābdī parve sānand bhakti-bhāve arpaṇ karavāmā āve chhe. (311-314)","english":"On the occasion of Pramukh Swami Maharaj’s birth centenary celebrations, this shastra is being offered with joy and devotion as a tribute to: (1) Parabrahman Sahajanand Shri Hari – the focus of upāsanā, (2) Mul Akshar Gunatitanand Swami, (3) Bhagatji Maharaj – the embodiment of wisdom, (4) Yagnapurushdasji (Shastriji Maharaj) – the protector of the true siddhānt, (5) the forever affectionate and blissful embodiment of Aksharbrahman, Yogiji Maharaj and (6) Guru Pramukh Swami Maharaj, who is humble and revered throughout the world. (311–314)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"313":{"sanskrit":["Vātsalyā’rdrā’tmane nityam ānanda-brahma-yogine;","Vishva-vandya-vinamrāya gurave Pramukhāya cha. 313"],"gujarati":"Upāsya Parabrahma Sahajānand Shrīhari tathā Mūḷ Akṣhar Guṇātītānand Swāmī, sākṣhād gnān-mūrti samā Bhagatjī Mahārāj, satya siddhāntnā rakṣhak evā Yagnapuruṣhdāsjī (Shāstrījī Mahārāj), sadāy vātsalya-bhīnā ane ānandmay brahma evā Yogījī Mahārāj tathā vishva-vandya ane vinamra evā guru Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājne ā shāstrarūpī anjali Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājnā janma shatābdī parve sānand bhakti-bhāve arpaṇ karavāmā āve chhe. (311-314)","english":"On the occasion of Pramukh Swami Maharaj’s birth centenary celebrations, this shastra is being offered with joy and devotion as a tribute to: (1) Parabrahman Sahajanand Shri Hari – the focus of upāsanā, (2) Mul Akshar Gunatitanand Swami, (3) Bhagatji Maharaj – the embodiment of wisdom, (4) Yagnapurushdasji (Shastriji Maharaj) – the protector of the true siddhānt, (5) the forever affectionate and blissful embodiment of Aksharbrahman, Yogiji Maharaj and (6) Guru Pramukh Swami Maharaj, who is humble and revered throughout the world. (311–314)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"314":{"sanskrit":["Anjalih shāstra-rūpo’yam sānandam bhakti-bhāvataha;","Arpyate Pramukha-Swāmi-janma-shatābdi-parvaṇi. 314"],"gujarati":"Upāsya Parabrahma Sahajānand Shrīhari tathā Mūḷ Akṣhar Guṇātītānand Swāmī, sākṣhād gnān-mūrti samā Bhagatjī Mahārāj, satya siddhāntnā rakṣhak evā Yagnapuruṣhdāsjī (Shāstrījī Mahārāj), sadāy vātsalya-bhīnā ane ānandmay brahma evā Yogījī Mahārāj tathā vishva-vandya ane vinamra evā guru Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājne ā shāstrarūpī anjali Pramukh Swāmī Mahārājnā janma shatābdī parve sānand bhakti-bhāve arpaṇ karavāmā āve chhe. (311-314)","english":"On the occasion of Pramukh Swami Maharaj’s birth centenary celebrations, this shastra is being offered with joy and devotion as a tribute to: (1) Parabrahman Sahajanand Shri Hari – the focus of upāsanā, (2) Mul Akshar Gunatitanand Swami, (3) Bhagatji Maharaj – the embodiment of wisdom, (4) Yagnapurushdasji (Shastriji Maharaj) – the protector of the true siddhānt, (5) the forever affectionate and blissful embodiment of Aksharbrahman, Yogiji Maharaj and (6) Guru Pramukh Swami Maharaj, who is humble and revered throughout the world. (311–314)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]},"315":{"sanskrit":["Tanotu sakale vishve paramānanda-mangalam;","Swāminārāyaṇah sākṣhād Akṣhara-Puruṣhottamaha. 315"],"gujarati":"Swāminārāyaṇ Bhagwān eṭale ke sākṣhāt Akṣhar-Puruṣhottam Mahārāj sakaḷ vishvamā param ānand-mangaḷne vistāre. (315)","english":"May Swaminarayan Bhagwan, that is, Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj himself,¹⁸ spread supreme bliss and auspiciousness throughout the entire world. (315)","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":["18. Here, Swaminarayan Bhagwan and Akshar-Purushottam Maharaj are synonyms and refer to the one supreme entity – Parabrahman, Paramatma."]},"316":{"sanskrit":["Iti Parabrahma-Swāminārāyaṇa-prabodhitā’gnopāsanasiddhānta-nirūpakam","prakaṭa-Brahmaswarūpa-Shrī-Mahanta-SwāmiMahārājaihi\nsva-hastā’ksharair-Gurjara-bhāshayā","likhitam Mahāmahopādhyāyena Sādhu-Bhadreshadāsena cha Sanskrita-shlokeshu","nibaddham Satsanga-Dīksheti shāstram sampūrṇam."],"gujarati":"Ām Parabrahma Bhagwān Shrī Swāminārāyaṇ dvārā prabodhit āgyā ane upāsanānā siddhāntonu nirūpaṇ karatu, Pragaṭ Brahmaswarūp Mahant Swāmī Mahārāj dvārā temanā potānā hastākṣharmā Gujarātīmā rachavāmā āvel ane Mahāmahopādhyāy Sādhu Bhadreshdās dvārā Sanskṛutmā shloka-baddha karavāmā āvel ‘Satsanga Dīkṣhā’ shāstra ahī samāpta thāy chhe.","english":"Thus concludes this ‘Satsang Diksha’ shastra which explains the principles of āgnā and upāsanā revealed by Parabrahma Swaminarayan. It has been written by Pragat Brahmaswarup Mahant Swami Maharaj in Gujarati in his own handwriting and rendered into Sanskrit verses by Mahamahopadhyay Sadhu Bhadreshdas.","gujFoot":[],"engFoot":[]}};
